# text = انا متكلمون الان فى صناعة الشعرا وانواعها ومخبرون اى قوة لكل واحد واحد منها وعلى اى سبيل ينبغى ان تتقوم الاسمار والاشعار ان كانت الفواسس مزمعة بان يجرى امرها مجرى الجودة وايضا من كم جزو هى وايما هى اجزاوها وكذلك نتكلم من اجل كم التى هى موجودة التى هى لها بعينها [ونتكلم] ونحن متكلمون فى هذا كله من حيث نبتدى اولا من الاشيا الاوايل
# transliteration = innā mutakallimūna l-āna fī ṣināʿati l-shuʿarāʾi wa-anwāʿihā wa-mukhbirūna ayya quwwatin li-kulli wāḥidin wāḥidin minhā wa-ʿalā ayyi sabīlin yanbaghī an tataqawwama l-asmāru wa-l-ashʿāru in kānati l-fawāsis muzmiʿatan bi-an yajriya amruhā majrā l-jūdati wa-ayḍan min kam juzʾin hiya wa-ayyumā hiya ajzāʾuhā wa-kadhālika natakallamu min ajli kam allatī hiya mawjūdatun allatī hiya lahā bi-ʿaynihā [wa-natakallamu] wa-naḥnu mutakallimūna fī hādhā kullihī min ḥaythu nabtadiʾu awwalan mina l-ashyāʾi l-awāʾili
# prose_translation = We are now speaking about the art of the poets and its kinds, and reporting what power belongs to each single one of them, and in what way the tales and the poems ought to be constituted if the poiesis is to run the course of excellence; and also of how many parts it consists, and which its parts are; and likewise we speak about how many are those [things] that exist, those that belong to it in itself [and we speak], we speaking about all this, inasmuch as we begin first from the first things.
# literal_translation = Verily-we [are] speaking now in the-art of-the-poets and-its-kinds, and-reporting which power to-each one one of-them, and-upon which way it-is-fitting that be-constituted the-tales and-the-poems, if was the-poiesis resolved to that runs its-affair the-course of-the-excellence; and-also of how-many part it [is], and-which [are] its-parts; and-likewise we-speak on-account-of how-many those-which they [are] existent, those-which they [are] to-it in-its-self [and-we-speak] and-we [are] speaking in this all-of-it, from where we-begin firstly from the-things the-first.
