# text = فكل شعر وكل نشيد شعرى ننحا به اما مديحا واما هجاا اما دثيرمبو الشعرى ونحو اكثر اوليطيقس وكل ما كان داخلا فى التشبه ومحاكاة صناعة الملاهى من الزمر والعود وغيره
# transliteration = fa-kullu shiʿrin wa-kullu nashīdin shiʿriyyin nanḥū bihī immā madīḥan wa-immā hijāʾan immā dīthīrambū l-shiʿriyyu wa-naḥwa akthari ūlīṭīqus wa-kullu mā kāna dākhilan fī l-tashabbuhi wa-muḥākāti ṣināʿati l-malāhī mina l-zamri wa-l-ʿūdi wa-ghayrihī
# prose_translation = Every poem, then, and every poetic song we direct either toward praise or toward lampoon; whether it be poetic dithyramb, or something like most of aulētikē, and everything that falls under likening and the imitation of the art of the instruments of play, of pipe and lute and the rest.
# literal_translation = So-every poem and-every song poetic we-direct with-it either praise or lampoon, either dithyramb the-poetic and-like most-of aulētikē, and-all what was entering in the-likening and-imitation of-the-art of-the-instruments, of the-pipe and-the-lute and-other-than-it.
