# translation_lang = en
# text = وكذلك ان كان الانسان يعمل الحكاية والتشبيه عند ما يخلط جميع الاوزان كما كان يعمل خاريمن فانه كن يشبه قانطورس برقص الدستبند من جميع الاوزان فقد يجب ان نلقبه شاعرا فمن قبل هذه كان حدد هذا الضرب
# transliteration = wa-kadhālika in kāna l-insānu yaʿmalu l-ḥikāyata wa-l-tashbīha ʿinda mā yakhliṭu jamīʿa l-awzāni kamā kāna yaʿmalu Khārīmun fa-innahū kāna yushabbihu Qānṭūrus bi-raqṣi l-dastband min jamīʿi l-awzāni fa-qad yajibu an nulaqqibahū shāʿiran fa-min qibali hādhihi kāna ḥuddida hādhā l-ḍarbu
# prose_translation = Likewise, if a man makes narration and likening while mixing all the metres, as Chaeremon used to do (for he likened the Centaur by the dastband dance, out of all the metres), then we must call him a poet. On these grounds, then, this kind has been defined.
# literal_translation = And-likewise if was the-man makes the-narration and-the-likening when he-mixes all the-metres, as was makes Chaeremon, so-verily-he was likens Centaur with-dance-of the-dastband from all the-metres, so-indeed it-is-necessary that we-call-him poet; so-from account-of these was defined this the-kind.
