# transliteration = wa-qad yūjadu qawmun yastaʿmilūna jamīʿa allatī wuṣifat mithālu dhālika fī l-laḥni wa-l-ṣawti l-ḥulwi wa-l-awzāni ka-ṣināʿati l-shiʿri allatī dīthūrambī wa-llatī li-l-nāṣūs wa-l-madīḥi ayḍan wa-l-hijāʾi wa-yakhtalifu bi-anna baʿḍahā maʿa l-kulli maʿan wa-baʿḍahā bi-l-juzʾi
# prose_translation = And there are people who use all the things described, for example melody, sweet voice and metres, as in the art of poetry that is dithyrambic (?) and that of the nomoi, and praise too, and lampoon; and they differ in that some use all together, and some part by part.
# literal_translation = And-indeed is-found people they-use all which were-described, example-of that in the-melody and-the-voice the-sweet and-the-metres, like-art-of the-poetry which [is] dithyrambic(?) and-which for-the-nomos, and-the-praise also and-the-lampoon; and-it-differs by-that some-of-them with the-all together, and-some-of-them by-the-part.
