# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 2.1
# translation_lang = en
# text = ولما كان الذين يحاكون ويشبهون قد ياتون بذلك بان يعملوا العمل الارادى فقد يجب ضرورة ان يكون هولا اما افاضل واما اراذل وذلك ان العادات والاخلاق مثلا هى تابعة لهذين فقط وذلك ان عادتهم واخلاقهم باجمعهم انما الخلاف بينها بالرذيلة والفضيلة وياتى بالحكاية والتشبيه اما الافاضل منا والاما [و]الاراذل واما من كانت حال فى ذلك كما يشبه المصورون فى صنايعهم اما الاخيار منهم للاخيار والاشرار للاشرار كما
# transliteration = wa-lammā kāna alladhīna yuḥākūna wa-yushabbihūna qad yaʾtūna bi-dhālika bi-an yaʿmalū l-ʿamala l-irādiyya fa-qad yajibu ḍarūratan an yakūna hāʾulāʾi immā afāḍila wa-immā arādhila wa-dhālika anna l-ʿādāti wa-l-akhlāqa mathalan hiya tābiʿatun li-hādhayni faqaṭ wa-dhālika anna ʿādatahum wa-akhlāqahum bi-ajmaʿihim innamā l-khilāfu baynahā bi-l-radhīlati wa-l-faḍīlati wa-yaʾtī bi-l-ḥikāyati wa-l-tashbīhi immā l-afāḍila minnā wa-l-immā(?) [wa-]l-arādhila wa-immā man kānat ḥālun fī dhālika kamā yushabbihu l-muṣawwirūna fī ṣanāʾiʿihim immā l-akhyāra minhum li-l-akhyāri wa-l-ashrāra li-l-ashrāri kamā
# prose_translation = Since those who imitate and liken bring this about by performing voluntary action, it is necessarily required that these be either virtuous or base; for habits and characters, for instance, follow these two alone, since the difference among the habits and characters of all of them lies only in vice and virtue. And [the imitator] produces narration and likening either of the virtuous among us, or (?) [and] of the base, or of those whose state in that [is ...], just as painters liken in their arts, either the good among them to the good and the bad to the bad, as
# literal_translation = And-when was those-who imitate and-liken indeed bring about-that by-that they-do the-action the-voluntary, so-indeed it-is-required necessarily that be these either virtuous or base; and-that [is] that the-habits and-the-characters for-example they [are] following to-these-two only; and-that [is] that their-habit and-their-characters in-their-entirety, only the-difference among-them [is] by-the-vice and-the-virtue; and-he-brings with-the-narration and-the-likening either the-virtuous of-us or(?) [and-]the-base, or whom was state in that, as liken the-painters in their-arts either the-good of-them to-the-good and-the-bad to-the-bad, as
