# text = وذلك ان فى هذه ايضا التشبيهات والحكايات هى هى باعيانها اما احيانا فمن حيث يوعدون التشبه اما بشى اخر يكون كما كان يفعل اوميروس او ان كان مثله الذى لا خلاف فيه ايضا وجميع الذين يعملون ويفعلون الذين يشبهون ويحاكون
# transliteration = wa-dhālika anna fī hādhihi ayḍan al-tashbīhāti wa-l-ḥikāyāti hiya hiya bi-aʿyānihā ammā aḥyānan fa-min ḥaythu yūʿidūna(?) l-tashabbuha immā bi-shayʾin ākhara yakūnu kamā kāna yafʿalu Ūmīrūs aw in kāna mithlahū alladhī lā khilāfa fīhi ayḍan wa-jamīʿu alladhīna yaʿmalūna wa-yafʿalūna alladhīna yushabbihūna wa-yuḥākūna
# prose_translation = For in these too the likenings and the narrations are the very same. Sometimes, inasmuch as they promise (?) the likening, either by some other thing that comes to be, as Homer used to do, or as if it were like him, the one in whom there is no change either; and all those who do and act are those who liken and imitate.
# literal_translation = And-that [is] that in these also the-likenings and-the-narrations, they [are] they in-their-selves; as-for sometimes, so-from where they-promise(?) the-likening, either by-thing other [that] comes-to-be, as was doing Homer, or if was like-him, which no difference in-it also; and-all those-who do and-act [are] those-who liken and-imitate.
