# sent_id = 3.4
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 3.4
# translation_lang = en
# text = وبهذه فمن الضرورة حتى يكون اما ذاك فهو مشبه ومحاكى واحد بعينه اما باوميروس سوفقلس وذلك ان كليهما يشبهان ويحاكيان الافاضل واما هذا فيشبهونه ويحاكونه شيعة ارسطوفانس من قبل انهم كانهم ويعملون ويفعلون كاٮٮٮٮهما ومن هاهنا قال قوم ان هذه تلقب ايضا دراماطا من قبل انهم يتشبهون بالذين يعملون
# transliteration = wa-bi-hādhihi fa-mina l-ḍarūrati ḥattā yakūna ammā dhāka fa-huwa mushabbihun wa-muḥākin wāḥidun bi-ʿaynihī ammā bi-Ūmīrūs Sūfaqlis wa-dhālika anna kilayhimā yushabbihāni wa-yuḥākiyāni l-afāḍila wa-ammā hādhā fa-yushabbihūnahū wa-yuḥākūnahū shīʿatu Arisṭūfānis min qibali annahum kaʾannahum wa-yaʿmalūna wa-yafʿalūna kā????humā(?) wa-min hāhunā qāla qawmun inna hādhihi tulaqqabu ayḍan drāmāṭā min qibali annahum yatashabbahūna bi-lladhīna yaʿmalūna
# prose_translation = By these, then, it is of necessity that, as for the one, he is one and the same likener and imitator (as for Sophocles, [he is] with Homer), for both of them liken and imitate the virtuous; and as for the other, the party of Aristophanes liken and imitate him, since they, as it were, do and act [...] (?). And hence some people have said that these are also called drāmāṭā, because they liken themselves to those who act.
# literal_translation = And-by-these so-from the-necessity that be, as-for that-one so-he [is] likener and-imitator one in-himself, as-for with-Homer Sophocles; and-that [is] that both-of-them liken and-imitate the-virtuous; and-as-for this-one so-they-liken-him and-they-imitate-him the-party-of Aristophanes, on account-of that-they as-if-they and-do and-act [...](?); and-from here said people that these are-called also dramata, on account-of that-they liken-themselves to-those-who act.
