# sent_id = 3.5
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 3.5
# translation_lang = en
# text = ولذلك صار اهل ادرياس هم متمسكون بالمديح والهجا اما بالهجا بحسب ما ظن فهذه التى هاهنا كما انه ما كان قبلهم ولاية الجماعة والتدبير والتى كان الذين من سيقلييا يقولون انها موجود كما كان يفعل افيخارمس الشاعر وهو الذى كان اقدم كثيرا من كيونيدس وماغنس [من حيث كانا اعطيا الرسوم]
# transliteration = wa-li-dhālika ṣāra ahlu Adriyās hum mutamassikūna bi-l-madīḥi wa-l-hijāʾi ammā bi-l-hijāʾi bi-ḥasabi mā ẓunna fa-hādhihi allatī hāhunā kamā annahū mā kāna qablahum wilāyatu l-jamāʿati wa-l-tadbīru wa-llatī kāna alladhīna min Sīqilliyā yaqūlūna innahā mawjūdun kamā kāna yafʿalu Afīkhārmus al-shāʿiru wa-huwa alladhī kāna aqdama kathīran min Kiyūnīdis wa-Māghnis [min ḥaythu kānā aʿṭayā l-rusūma]
# prose_translation = Therefore the people of Adriyās (the Dorians) came to hold fast to praise and lampoon. As for lampoon, according to what has been supposed, [it is] these here, as though there had not (?) been before them the rule of the community and administration; and that which those from Sicily used to say exists, as Epicharmus the poet used to do, he who was much older than Chionides and Magnes [inasmuch as the two had given the names (?)].
# literal_translation = And-for-that became people-of Adriyās, they [are] holding-fast to-the-praise and-the-lampoon; as-for with-the-lampoon, according-to what was-supposed, so-these which [are] here, as that-it not was before-them rule-of the-community and-the-administration; and-which was those-who [are] from Sicily saying that-it [is] existent, as was doing Epicharmus the-poet, and-he [is] who was older much than Chionides and-Magnes [from where they-two-had given the-names].
