# text = عند ما كانا يستعملان الاقرار من اسما المديح التى فى فالوفونيهوس وذلك ان [انه] اما ذانك لقبا لقرى قومانس واما ديموسوس فلقب اهل اثينية المهجوين من قبل انهم كانوا ممتهنين مستخف بهم من اهل القرى
# transliteration = ʿinda mā kānā yastaʿmilāni l-iqrāra min asmāʾi l-madīḥi allatī fī Fālūfūnīhūs wa-dhālika anna [annahū] ammā dhānika laqqabā li-quran qūmānis wa-ammā dīmūsūs fa-laqqaba ahla Athīniyata l-mahjuwwīna min qibali annahum kānū mumtahanīna mustakhaffan bihim min ahli l-qurā
# prose_translation = when the two used to employ, as evidence (?), the names of praise that are in the Peloponnese: for, as for those two, they called the villages kōmai, and as for dēmoi, [one] so named the lampooned people of Athens, because they were despised and made light of by the people of the villages.
# literal_translation = When was they-two-using the-avowal from names-of the-praise which [are] in Peloponnese; and-that [is] that [that-it] as-for those-two they-named to-villages kōmas, and-as-for dēmos so-he-named people-of Athens the-lampooned, on account-of that-they were despised made-light of-them by people-of the-villages.
