# sent_id = 4.2
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 4.2
# translation_lang = en
# text = والتشبيه والمحاكاة مما ينشوا مع الناس منذ اول الامر وهم اطفال وهذا مما يخالف به الناس الحيوانات الاخر من قبل ان الانسان يشبه ويستعمل المحاكاة اكثر ويتتلمذ ويجعل التلمذات بالتشبيه والمحاكاة للاشيا المتقدمة والاوايل وذلك ان جميعهم يسر ويفرح بالتشبيه والمحاكاة
# transliteration = wa-l-tashbīhu wa-l-muḥākātu mimmā yanshaʾu maʿa l-nāsi mundhu awwali l-amri wa-hum aṭfālun wa-hādhā mimmā yukhālifu bihī l-nāsu l-ḥayawānāti l-ukhara min qibali anna l-insāna yushabbihu wa-yastaʿmilu l-muḥākāta akthara wa-yatatalmadhu wa-yajʿalu l-talmadhāti bi-l-tashbīhi wa-l-muḥākāti li-l-ashyāʾi l-mutaqaddimati wa-l-awāʾili wa-dhālika anna jamīʿahum yusarru wa-yafraḥu bi-l-tashbīhi wa-l-muḥākāti
# prose_translation = Likening and imitation are among the things that grow up with people from the very beginning, while they are children; and this is among the things by which people differ from the other animals, since man likens and uses imitation most, and learns, and makes his lessons by likening and imitation of the prior and first things; and that is because all of them are delighted and glad at likening and imitation.
# literal_translation = And-the-likening and-the-imitation [are] of-what grows with the-people since first-of the-matter, and-they [are] children; and-this [is] of-what differ by-it the-people the-animals the-other, on account-of that the-man likens and-uses the-imitation more, and-becomes-a-pupil and-makes the-lessons by-the-likening and-the-imitation of-the-things the-prior and-the-first; and-that [is] that all-of-them is-delighted and-rejoices at-the-likening and-the-imitation.
