# text = والدليل على ذلك هذا وهو الذى يعرض فى الافعال ايضا وذلك ان التى نراها ويكون روساها على جهة الاغتمام فانا نسر بصورتها وتماثيلها اما اذا نحن رايناها كالتى هى اشد استقصا مثال ذلك صور وخلق الحيوانات المهينة المايتة
# transliteration = wa-l-dalīlu ʿalā dhālika hādhā wa-huwa alladhī yaʿriḍu fī l-afʿāli ayḍan wa-dhālika anna allatī narāhā wa-yakūnu ruʾūsuhā(?) ʿalā jihati l-ightimāmi fa-innā nusarru bi-ṣūratihā wa-tamāthīlihā ammā idhā naḥnu raʾaynāhā ka-llatī hiya ashaddu istiqṣāʾan mithālu dhālika ṣuwaru wa-khalqu l-ḥayawānāti l-mahīnati l-māʾitati
# prose_translation = The evidence of this is the following, namely what happens with actions too: the things that we see, and whose heads (?) are in a state of distress, we take delight in their images and statues, that is, when we see them as the most exactly rendered; for example the forms and shapes of the lowliest, dead animals.
# literal_translation = And-the-evidence of that [is] this, and-it [is] which occurs in the-actions also; and-that [is] that which we-see-them and-are their-heads(?) upon manner-of the-distress, so-verily-we are-delighted by-their-image and-their-statues, as-for when we saw-them as-which they [are] most exactness; example-of that [are] forms and-shapes-of the-animals the-lowly the-dead.
