# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 4.7
# translation_lang = en
# text = واما بالطبع فلنا ان نتشبه بالتاليف واللحون وذلك انه اما ان الاوزان مشابهات للالحان فهو بين للذين هم مفطورون على ذلك منذ الابتدا وخاصة انهم ولدوا صناعة الشعر من حيث ياتون بذلك ويمتعون قليلا قليلا وولدوها من الذين اٮفوها دفعة ومن ساعته
# transliteration = wa-ammā bi-l-ṭabʿi fa-lanā an natashabbaha bi-l-taʾlīfi wa-l-luḥūni wa-dhālika annahū ammā anna l-awzāna mushābihātun li-l-alḥāni fa-huwa bayyinun li-lladhīna hum mafṭūrūna ʿalā dhālika mundhu l-ibtidāʾi wa-khāṣṣatan annahum walladū ṣināʿata l-shiʿri min ḥaythu yaʾtūna bi-dhālika wa-yumtiʿūna(?) qalīlan qalīlan wa-walladūhā mina lladhīna a?fūhā(?) dafʿatan wa-min sāʿatihī
# prose_translation = As for [what is] by nature: it belongs to us to liken by composition and melodies; for, that metres are similar to melodies is clear to those who are naturally disposed to this from the beginning, and above all [it is clear] that they generated the art of poetry, inasmuch as they produce this and give delight (?) little by little, and generated it out of those who [...] (?) it all at once and on the spot.
# literal_translation = And-as-for by-the-nature, so-to-us that we-liken by-the-composition and-the-melodies; and-that [is] that-it, as-for that the-metres [are] similar to-the-melodies, so-it [is] clear to-those-who they [are] disposed upon that since the-beginning, and-especially that-they generated art-of the-poetry, from where they-bring about-that and-delight(?) little little, and-generated-it from those-who ?-ed-it(?) at-once and-from its-hour.
