# sent_id = 4.8
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 4.8
# translation_lang = en
# text = وانجذبت بحسب عادتها الخاصية اعنى صناعة الشعر وذلك ان بعض الشعرا ومن كان منهم اكثر عفافا يتشبهون بالاعمال الحسنة الجميلة وفى ما اشبه ذلك وبعضهم ممن قد كان منهم ارذل عند ما كانوا يهجون اولا الاشرار كانوا يعملون بعد ذلك المديح والثنا لقوم اخرين اشرار
# transliteration = wa-njadhabat bi-ḥasabi ʿādatihā l-khāṣṣiyyati aʿnī ṣināʿata l-shiʿri wa-dhālika anna baʿḍa l-shuʿarāʾi wa-man kāna minhum akthara ʿafāfan yatashabbahūna bi-l-aʿmāli l-ḥasanati l-jamīlati wa-fī mā ashbaha dhālika wa-baʿḍuhum mimman qad kāna minhum ardhala ʿinda mā kānū yahjūna awwalan al-ashrāra kānū yaʿmalūna baʿda dhālika l-madīḥa wa-l-thanāʾa li-qawmin ākharīna ashrārin
# prose_translation = And it (I mean the art of poetry) was drawn apart according to its proper character: some of the poets, those of them who were more chaste, liken [themselves] to fine and beautiful actions and to what resembles them; and some of them, of those who were baser, having at first lampooned the wicked, afterwards used to make praise and eulogy for other people, wicked ones.
# literal_translation = And-it-was-drawn according-to its-habit the-proper, I-mean art-of the-poetry; and-that [is] that some-of the-poets and-who was of-them more chastity liken-themselves to-the-actions the-fine the-beautiful and-in what resembled that; and-some-of-them, of-whom indeed was of-them baser, when they-were lampooning first the-wicked, they-were making after that the-praise and-the-eulogy for-people other wicked.
