# sent_id = 4.12
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 4.12
# translation_lang = en
# text = كما ان الشاعر فى الاشيا الحريصة المجتهدة خاصة انما كان اوميروس وحده فقط وذلك انه هو وحده فقط ليس انما عمل اشيا احسن فيها لكن قد عمل التشبيهات والحكايات المعروفة بدماطيقياتا وهكذى هو اول من اظهر شكل صناعة هجا ليس فيه الهجا فقط لكن فى باب الاستهزا والمطانزة فانه عمل فيها النشيد المسما باليونانية دراماطا وذلك ان هارلٮلوٮا حالها حال يجرى مجرى التسقيم فكما ان ايليادا عند الركب والمسماة اودوسيا غير المديحات كذلك هذا عند ابواب الهجا
# transliteration = kamā anna l-shāʿira fī l-ashyāʾi l-ḥarīṣati l-mujtahidati khāṣṣatan innamā kāna Ūmīrūs waḥdahū faqaṭ wa-dhālika annahū huwa waḥdahū faqaṭ laysa innamā ʿamila ashyāʾa aḥsana fīhā lākin qad ʿamila l-tashbīhāti wa-l-ḥikāyāti l-maʿrūfata bi-dmāṭīqiyātā wa-hākadhā huwa awwalu man aẓhara shakla ṣināʿati hijāʾin laysa fīhi l-hijāʾu faqaṭ lākin fī bābi l-istihzāʾi wa-l-muṭānazati fa-innahū ʿamila fīhā l-nashīda l-musammā bi-l-yūnāniyyati drāmāṭā wa-dhālika anna Hārl?lū?ā ḥāluhā ḥālun yajrī majrā l-tasqīmi(?) fa-kamā anna Īliyādā ʿinda l-rakbi(?) wa-l-musammāta Ūdūsiyā ghayru(?) l-madīḥāti kadhālika hādhā ʿinda abwābi l-hijāʾi
# prose_translation = Just as in earnest and diligent matters the poet above all was Homer alone (for he alone not only made better things in them, but also made the likenings and narrations known as dramatic), so too he was the first to show the shape of an art of lampoon in which there is not lampoon only, but [which lies] in the domain of mockery and jesting; for he made in it the song called in Greek drāmāṭā. For the Margites (?): its state is a state that runs the course of [...] (?); for just as the Iliad in relation to the riders (?), and the one called Odyssey, are other than (?) the praises, so is this in relation to the forms of lampoon.
# literal_translation = As that the-poet in the-things the-earnest the-diligent especially only was Homer alone-he only; and-that [is] that-he, he alone-he only, not only made things better in-them, but indeed made the-likenings and-the-narrations the-known as-dramatic; and-thus he [is] first-of who showed shape-of art-of lampoon, not in-it the-lampoon only, but in domain-of the-mockery and-the-jesting; so-verily-he made in-it the-song the-named in-the-Greek drama; and-that [is] that Margites(?), its-state [is] state [that] runs course-of the-?; so-as that Iliad with the-riders(?) and-the-named Odyssey [are] other-than(?) the-praises, likewise this [is] with forms-of the-lampoon.
