# sent_id = 4.13
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 4.13
# translation_lang = en
# text = ولما ظهرا [مد] مذهب [الهجا و]المديح ومذهب الهجا فالذين نحوا وقصدوا به بصناعة الشعر كلتى هاتين بحسب خصوصية الطبع بعضهم كانوا يعملون مكان المذهب من الشعر المسمى ايامبو ابواب الهجا وبعضهم كانوا يعملون مكان هذه التى للمسماة افيس ابواب المديح وصاروا معلمين لذلك من قبل انه قد كانت هذه اعظم كثيرا واشرف فى شكل هذه فانه ان ٮعمل هو هو مبدا الصناعة المديح وبالانواع على الكفاية وذلك انه اما ان تكون تانك ٮحيٮں بهذه او يكون عند كلتيهما بنسبة اخرى
# transliteration = wa-lammā ẓaharā [mad] madhhabu [l-hijāʾi wa-]l-madīḥi wa-madhhabu l-hijāʾi fa-lladhīna naḥaw wa-qaṣadū bihī bi-ṣināʿati l-shiʿri kiltā hātayni bi-ḥasabi khuṣūṣiyyati l-ṭabʿi baʿḍuhum kānū yaʿmalūna makāna l-madhhabi mina l-shiʿri l-musammā iyāmbū abwāba l-hijāʾi wa-baʿḍuhum kānū yaʿmalūna makāna hādhihi allatī li-l-musammāti afīs abwāba l-madīḥi wa-ṣārū muʿallimīna li-dhālika min qibali annahū qad kānat hādhihi aʿẓama kathīran wa-ashrafa fī shakli hādhihi fa-innahū in yaʿmal(?) huwa huwa mabdaʾu l-ṣināʿati l-madīḥi wa-bi-l-anwāʿi ʿalā l-kifāyati wa-dhālika annahū immā an takūna tānika ?ḥy?n(?) bi-hādhihi aw yakūna ʿinda kiltayhimā bi-nisbatin ukhrā
# prose_translation = And when the school of praise and the school of lampoon appeared, those who aimed at it and intended it with the art of poetry, [in] both of these, according to the particular character of [their] nature: some of them used to make, in place of the school of poetry called iambos, forms of lampoon, and some of them used to make, in place of what belongs to the [poetry] called epic (afīs), forms of praise; and they became teachers of that, because these were much greater and nobler in shape than (?) those. For if one does [so] (?), it is itself the principle of the art of praise, and [furnished] with the kinds sufficiently; namely, either those two [...] (?) by these, or it is, in relation to both of them, by another relation.
# literal_translation = And-when appeared-the-two [...] school-of [the-lampoon and-]the-praise and-school-of the-lampoon, so-those-who aimed and-intended at-it with-art-of the-poetry, both-of these-two, according-to particularity-of the-nature, some-of-them were making in-place-of the-school of the-poetry the-named iambos forms-of the-lampoon, and-some-of-them were making in-place-of these which [are] to-the-named epic forms-of the-praise; and-they-became teachers of-that, on account-of that-it indeed were these greater much and-nobler in shape-of these; so-verily-it, if he-does(?), it it [is] principle-of the-art the-praise, and-with-the-kinds upon the-sufficiency; and-that [is] that-it either that be those-two [...](?) with-these, or be with both-of-them by-relation other.
