# sent_id = 4.18
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 4.18
# translation_lang = en
# text = واما مٮدلدں العامل فكانوا يستعملون رباعية الوزن بسبب الرقص المعروف بساطورانقى لكيما يتشبه به الشعر اكثروا عند ما كانت تنشوا مقولة وكلام فالطبيعة كانت تجد وزنها ولا سيما من قبل ان الوزن كان يعمل الاخر اٮـ*سها وقد يجارى بعضنا بعضا بالمخاطبة والمكايلة دليل هذه السبيل
# transliteration = wa-ammā m?dld?(?) al-ʿāmili fa-kānū yastaʿmilūna rubāʿiyyata l-wazni bi-sababi l-raqṣi l-maʿrūfi bi-sāṭūrānqī li-kaymā yatashabbaha bihī l-shiʿru aktharū ʿinda mā kānat tanshaʾu maqūlatun wa-kalāmun fa-l-ṭabīʿatu kānat tajidu waznahā wa-lā siyyamā min qibali anna l-wazna kāna yaʿmalu l-ākhara a**sahā wa-qad yujārī baʿḍunā baʿḍan bi-l-mukhāṭabati wa-l-mukāyalati dalīlu hādhihi l-sabīli
# prose_translation = As for [...] (?) of the maker, they used to employ the tetrameter on account of the dance known as satyric, so that poetry might be likened by it; they did so more (?). When utterance and speech were arising, nature used to find its metre, especially because the metre used to make the other [...]; and some of us keep pace with one another in address and exchange. The evidence of this way:
# literal_translation = And-as-for [...](?) the-maker, so-they-were using quadruple-of the-metre by-cause-of the-dance the-known as-satyric, so-that be-likened by-it the-poetry; they-did-more(?); when was arising utterance and-speech, so-the-nature was finding its-metre, and-not like-what [= especially] on account-of that the-metre was making the-other [...]; and-indeed keeps-pace some-of-us some by-the-address and-the-exchange; evidence-of this the-way:
