# translation_lang = en
# text = فصناعة المديح هى تشبيه ومحاكاة للعمل الارادى الحريص والكامل التى لها عظم ومداد فى القول النافع ما خلال كل واحد واحد من الانواع التى هى فاعلة فى الاجزا لا بالمواعيد وتعدل الانفعالات والتاثيرات بالرحمة والخوف وتنقى وتنظف الذين يفعلون ويعمل
# transliteration = fa-ṣināʿatu l-madīḥi hiya tashbīhun wa-muḥākātun li-l-ʿamali l-irādiyyi l-ḥarīṣi wa-l-kāmili allatī lahā ʿiẓamun wa-madādun fī l-qawli l-nāfiʿi mā khilāla kulli wāḥidin wāḥidin mina l-anwāʿi allatī hiya fāʿilatun fī l-ajzāʾi lā bi-l-mawāʿīdi wa-tuʿaddilu l-infiʿālāti wa-l-taʾthīrāti bi-l-raḥmati wa-l-khawfi wa-tunaqqī wa-tunaẓẓifu alladhīna yafʿalūna wa-yaʿmalu
# prose_translation = The art of praise, then, is a likening and imitation of the voluntary, earnest and complete action, which has magnitude and extent (?), in useful speech, apart (?) from each single one of the kinds that are active in the parts, not by promises; and it moderates the passions and affections by pity and fear, and purifies and cleanses those who act, and he makes (?).
# literal_translation = So-art-of the-praise it [is] likening and-imitation of-the-action the-voluntary the-earnest and-the-complete, which to-it [is] magnitude and-extent(?), in the-speech the-useful, except(?) each one one of the-kinds which they [are] acting in the-parts, not by-the-promises; and-it-moderates the-passions and-the-affections by-the-pity and-the-fear, and-it-purifies and-it-cleanses those-who act, and-he-makes(?).
