# translation_lang = en
# text = من قبل انه تشبيه ومحاكاة للعمل ويعرضها من قوم يعرضون التى تدعوا الضرورة اليها مثل اى اناس يكونوا فى عاٮاتهم واعتقادتهم وذلك ان بهذه نقول ان الاحاديث تكون وكم هى وكيف حالها وعلل الاحاديث والقصص اثنتا وهما العادات والارا وان بحسب توجد الاحاديث والقصص من حيث يستقيم كلها بهذين وتزل بهما
# transliteration = min qibali annahū tashbīhun wa-muḥākātun li-l-ʿamali wa-yaʿriḍuhā min qawmin yaʿriḍūna allatī tadʿū l-ḍarūratu ilayhā mithla ayyi unāsin yakūnū fī ʿādātihum(?) wa-iʿtiqādātihum wa-dhālika anna bi-hādhihi naqūlu anna l-aḥādītha takūnu wa-kam hiya wa-kayfa ḥāluhā wa-ʿilalu l-aḥādīthi wa-l-qiṣaṣi ithnatā wa-humā l-ʿādātu wa-l-ārāʾu wa-anna bi-ḥasabi tūjadu l-aḥādīthu wa-l-qiṣaṣu min ḥaythu yastaqīmu kulluhā bi-hādhayni wa-tazillu bihumā
# prose_translation = Since it is a likening and imitation of action, and [one] presents it by means of people who present what necessity calls for, such as what sort of people they are in their habits (?) and their beliefs; for it is by these that we say the stories come to be, and how many they are, and what their state is; and the causes of the stories and tales are two, namely the habits and the opinions; and that according to [these] the stories and tales are found, inasmuch as all of them go right by these two and slip by them.
# literal_translation = From account-of that-it [is] likening and-imitation of-the-action, and-presents-it from people they-present which calls the-necessity to-it, like which people they-be in their-habits(?) and-their-beliefs; and-that [is] that by-these we-say that the-stories are, and-how-many they [are], and-how [is] their-state; and-causes-of the-stories and-the-tales [are] two, and-they-two [are] the-habits and-the-opinions; and-that according-to are-found the-stories and-the-tales, from where goes-right all-of-them by-these-two and-slips by-them-two.
