# transliteration = wa-aʿẓamu min qiwāmi l-umūri min qibali anna ṣināʿata l-madīḥi hiya tashabbuhun wa-ḥikāyatun lā li-l-nāsi lākin bi-aʿmālin(?) wa-l-ḥayāti wa-l-**** hiya fī l-ʿamali wa-hiya amrun huwa kamālun mā wa-ʿamalun mā wa-hum ammā bi-ḥasabi l-ʿādāti fa-yushabbihūna kayfa kānū wa-ammā bi-ḥasabi l-aʿmāli fa-l-fāʾizīna aw bi-l-ʿaksi
# prose_translation = And greater (?) is the constitution of the matters, because the art of praise is a likening and narration not of people but by (?) actions and life; and the […] is in action; and it is a matter that is a certain perfection and a certain action. As for them: according to the habits, they liken how they were; and according to the actions, [they liken] the successful ones, or the reverse.
# literal_translation = And-greater from constitution-of the-matters, from account-of that art-of the-praise it [is] likening and-narration, not of-the-people but by-actions(?) and-the-life; and-the-[…] it [is] in the-action; and-it [is] matter it [is] perfection some and-action some; and-they, as-for according-to the-habits, so-they-liken how they-were, and-as-for according-to the-actions, so-the-successful, or by-the-reverse.
