# text = من قبل ان مديحات الصبيان اكثرها بلا اعادة وبالجملة الشعرا الاخر هم بهذه الحال كالحال فيما كان عن زوكسيدس المكتت عند ما دونه الى فراغنوطس من قبل ان ذاك رجل قد كان يكتب عادات جياد خيرة واما ما دونه وكسيدس فليس فيه عادة ما
# transliteration = min qibali anna madīḥāti l-ṣibyāni aktharuhā bi-lā iʿādatin wa-bi-l-jumlati l-shuʿarāʾu l-ukharu hum bi-hādhihi l-ḥāli ka-l-ḥāli fī mā kāna ʿan Zūksīdis al-muktati ʿinda mā dawwanahū ilā Farāghnūṭis min qibali anna dhāka rajulun qad kāna yaktubu ʿādātin jiyādan khayyiratan wa-ammā mā dawwanahū Wuksīdis fa-laysa fīhi ʿādatun mā
# prose_translation = For the praise-poems of the young are for the most part without repetition (?), and in general the other poets are in this condition, as was the case with Zeuxis the (?) painter when he recorded [his work] in comparison with Polygnotus: that one was a man who used to write good and excellent habits, whereas what Zeuxis recorded has no habit at all.
# literal_translation = From account-of that praise-poems-of the-boys, most-of-them [are] with-no repetition; and-in-the-sum the-poets the-other they [are] in-this the-state, like-the-state in-what was from Zeuxis the-?painter when he-recorded-it to Polygnotus; from account-of that that-one [was] man indeed was writes habits good excellent; and-as-for what recorded-it Zeuxis, so-not-is in-it habit any.
