# text = ومتى ولما كان الطبيعة الامور قد يظن انه يوجد الى ان يظهر كان هذا من الافضل فى العظم وكما حدوا على الاطلاق وقالوا فى كم من العظم على الحقيقة او تلك تدعوا الضرورة عند ما تكون فى هذه التى تكون على الاضطرار واحد فى اثر الاخر تنوب عند النجاح الكاين بعد رداوة البخت او تغير رداوة البخت الى الصلاح يكون العظم حد كافى
# transliteration = wa-matā wa-lammā kāna l-ṭabīʿatu l-umūri qad yuẓannu annahū yūjadu ilā an yaẓhara kāna hādhā mina l-afḍali fī l-ʿiẓami wa-kamā ḥaddū ʿalā l-iṭlāqi wa-qālū fī kam mina l-ʿiẓami ʿalā l-ḥaqīqati aw tilka tadʿū l-ḍarūratu ʿinda mā takūnu fī hādhihi allatī takūnu ʿalā l-iḍṭirāri wāḥidun fī athari l-ākhari tanūbu ʿinda l-najāḥi l-kāʾini baʿda radāʾati l-bakhti aw taghayyuri radāʾati l-bakhti ilā l-ṣalāḥi yakūnu l-ʿiẓamu ḥaddan kāfiyan
# prose_translation = And when, since by the nature of the matters it is thought to exist until it becomes manifest, this was the better in magnitude. And as they defined absolutely, and said: in how much magnitude, in truth or as necessity calls for, when [things] are in these [events] that are by necessity one after another, [fortune] alternates at the success that comes after ill fortune, or at the change of ill fortune to good, the magnitude is a sufficient limit.
# literal_translation = And-when and-since was the-nature the-matters indeed is-thought that-it is-found until that it-appears, was this of the-better in the-magnitude; and-as they-defined upon the-absoluteness and-they-said: in how-much of the-magnitude upon the-truth or that calls the-necessity, when they-are in these which are upon the-necessity one in trace-of the-other, alternates at the-success the-being after badness-of the-fortune or change-of badness-of the-fortune to the-good, is the-magnitude limit sufficient.
