# sent_id = 8.3
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 8.3
# translation_lang = en
# text = واما اوميروس فانه كما انه بينه وبينهم فرق فى اشيا اخر وهذا يشبه ان يكون فى نظره نظرا جيدا اما بسبب الصناعة واما من اجل الطبيعة وذلك انه لما دون امر اودوسيا لم يثبت كل ما عرض لاودوسوس بمنزلة الضربة وهذه [و]الشرور والغير التى كانت فى فارناوسوس والسخط الذى سخطوا عليه فى الحرب الذى كان عند اغارومس ولا ايضا كل واحد واحد من الاشيا عرضت مما كانت الضرورة تدعوا الى ان يثبت فى المٮال لكن ما دونه بان قصد به نحو عمل واحد وهو المسمى اودوسيا المنسوب الى اودوسوس وكذلك فعل فى ما دونه من امر ايليادا
# transliteration = wa-ammā Ūmīrūs fa-innahū kamā annahū baynahū wa-baynahum farqun fī ashyāʾa ukhara wa-hādhā yushbihu an yakūna fī naẓarihī naẓaran jayyidan immā bi-sababi l-ṣināʿati wa-immā min ajli l-ṭabīʿati wa-dhālika annahū lammā dawwana amra Ūdūsiyā lam yuthbit kulla mā ʿaraḍa li-Ūdūsūs bi-manzilati l-ḍarbati wa-hādhihi [wa-]l-shurūri wa-l-ghiyari allatī kānat fī Fārnāwusūs wa-l-sukhṭi alladhī sakhiṭū ʿalayhi fī l-ḥarbi alladhī kāna ʿinda Aghārūmus wa-lā ayḍan kulla wāḥidin wāḥidin mina l-ashyāʾi ʿaraḍat mimmā kānati l-ḍarūratu tadʿū ilā an yuthbita fī l-mithāli(?) lākin mā dawwanahū bi-an qaṣada bihī naḥwa ʿamalin wāḥidin wa-huwa l-musammā Ūdūsiyā l-mansūbu ilā Ūdūsūs wa-kadhālika faʿala fī mā dawwanahū min amri Īliyādā
# prose_translation = As for Homer: just as there is a difference between him and them in other things, so he seems in this to have had a good view, whether owing to art or on account of nature. For when he recorded the story of the Odyssey he did not set down everything that befell Odysseus, such as the blow, and these [and] evils and vicissitudes that were at Parnassus, and the anger with which they were angry at him in the war that was at Agharumus; nor, again, each single one of the things that befell, of what necessity was calling to be set down in the example (?); but what he recorded, [he recorded] by aiming with it at one action, namely the one called "Odyssey", attributed to Odysseus; and he did likewise in what he recorded of the story of the Iliad.
# literal_translation = And-as-for Homer, so-verily-he: as that-it between-him and-between-them [is] difference in things other, and-this seems that be in his-view view good, either because-of the-art or on-account-of the-nature; and-that [is] that-he when recorded story-of Odyssey not set-down all what befell to-Odysseus, like-the-blow and-these [and-]the-evils and-the-vicissitudes which were in Parnassus, and-the-anger which they-were-angry upon-him in the-war which was at Agharumus; and-not also each one one of the-things befell, of-what was the-necessity calls to that he-set-down in the-example(?); but what he-recorded-it, by-that he-aimed with-it toward action one, and-it [is] the-named Odyssey the-attributed to Odysseus; and-likewise he-did in what he-recorded-it of story-of Iliad.
