# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 9.1
# translation_lang = en
# text = وظاهر مما قيل ان التى كانت مثلا ليست من فعل الشاعر لكن ذلك انما فى مثل اى شى يكون اما ما هو الممكن من ذلك على الحقيقة واما التى تدعوا الضرورة اليه
# transliteration = wa-ẓāhirun mimmā qīla anna allatī kānat mathalan laysat min fiʿli l-shāʿiri lākin dhālika innamā fī mithli ayyi shayʾin yakūnu immā mā huwa l-mumkinu min dhālika ʿalā l-ḥaqīqati wa-immā allatī tadʿū l-ḍarūratu ilayhi
# prose_translation = It is evident from what has been said that the things that have happened, for example, are not the poet's doing; rather, that lies only in the like of whatever thing may be: either what is possible of that in truth, or what necessity calls for.
# literal_translation = And-evident from-what was-said that which were, for-example, are-not of doing-of the-poet; but that [is] only in like-of which thing is, either what it [is] the-possible of that upon the-truth, or which calls the-necessity to-it.
