# sent_id = 9.2
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 9.2
# translation_lang = en
# text = وذلك ان الذى يثبت الاحاديث والقصص والشاعر ايضا وان كانا يتكلمان هكذى بالوزن وبغير وزن هما مختلفان وذلك ان لايرودوطس ان يكون بالوزن وليس لما يدون ويكتب ان يكون مع الوزن او بغير وزن باقل لكن هذا يخالف بان ذاك يقول الى تقال واما هذا فاى الاشيا كانت
# transliteration = wa-dhālika anna alladhī yuthbitu l-aḥādītha wa-l-qiṣaṣa wa-l-shāʿira ayḍan wa-in kānā yatakallamāni hākadhā bi-l-wazni wa-bi-ghayri waznin humā mukhtalifāni wa-dhālika anna li-Īrūdūṭus an yakūna bi-l-wazni wa-laysa li-mā yudawwanu wa-yuktabu an yakūna maʿa l-wazni aw bi-ghayri waznin bi-aqalla lākin hādhā yukhālifu bi-anna dhāka yaqūlu allatī(?) tuqālu wa-ammā hādhā fa-ayya l-ashyāʾi kānat
# prose_translation = For the one who records reports and stories, and the poet too, even if both speak thus in metre and without metre, are different [from each other]. For it is possible for Herodotus to be in metre, and what is recorded and written is not any the less [such] whether it is with metre or without metre; but this one differs in that that one says what is said (?), while this one [says] whatever things there were.
# literal_translation = And-that [is] that who records the-reports and-the-stories, and-the-poet also, and-if were-two they-two-speak thus with-the-metre and-with-other-than metre, they-two [are] differing; and-that [is] that to-Herodotus that it-be with-the-metre, and-not-is to-what is-recorded and-is-written that it-be with the-metre or with-other-than metre by-less; but this differs by-that that-one says which(?) is-said, and-as-for this-one, so-which-of the-things were.
