# sent_id = 9.4
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 9.4
# translation_lang = en
# text = وهى بالكلية والتى فى الكيفية والمكيفيات كل التى كانها تعرض ان تقال او تعمل اما التى بالحقيقة واما التى هى ضرورية كالتوهم الذى يكون فى صناعة الشعر عند ما تكون صناعة الشعر نفسها تضع الاسما [فى] فالوحيدات والجزويات مثلا هى ان يقال ماذا فعل الفسادس اما الذى انفعل
# transliteration = wa-hiya bi-l-kulliyyati wa-llatī fī l-kayfiyyati wa-l-mukayyafāti kullu allatī ka-annahā taʿriḍu an tuqāla aw tuʿmala immā allatī bi-l-ḥaqīqati wa-immā allatī hiya ḍarūriyyatun ka-l-tawahhumi alladhī yakūnu fī ṣināʿati l-shiʿri ʿinda mā takūnu ṣināʿatu l-shiʿri nafsuhā taḍaʿu l-asmāʾa [fī] fa-l-waḥīdātu wa-l-juzʾiyyātu mathalan hiya an yuqāla mādhā faʿala Alfasādis immā alladhī infaʿala
# prose_translation = It is by way of the universal; and what concerns the quality and the qualified things is everything that, as it were, happens to be said or done, either what is according to truth or what is necessary, like the conjecture that is in the art of poetry when the art of poetry itself assigns the names [in]. The singulars and particulars, for example, are that one should say what Alcibiades did, or (?) what he suffered.
# literal_translation = And-it [is] by-the-universality; and-which [is] in the-quality and-the-qualified [is] all which as-if-it happens that it-be-said or be-done, either which [is] by-the-truth or which it [is] necessary, like-the-conjecture which is in art-of the-poetry when is art-of the-poetry itself puts the-names [in]; so-the-singulars and-the-particulars, for-example, it [is] that is-said what did Alcibiades, or(?) which he-suffered.
