# text = من قبل ان فى صناعة المديح كانوا يتمسكون بالاسما التى كانت والسبب فى هذا هو ان الحال الممكنة هى مقنعة والتى لم تكن بعد فلسنا نصدق انها يمكن ان تكون واما التى قد كانت توجد ان كان قد كانت موجودة فلا يمكن الا تكون
# transliteration = min qibali anna fī ṣināʿati l-madīḥi kānū yatamassakūna bi-l-asmāʾi allatī kānat wa-l-sababu fī hādhā huwa anna l-ḥāla l-mumkinata hiya muqniʿatun wa-llatī lam takun baʿdu fa-lasnā nuṣaddiqu annahā yumkinu an takūna wa-ammā allatī qad kānat tūjadu in kāna qad kānat mawjūdatan fa-lā yumkinu allā takūna
# prose_translation = because in the art of praise they used to hold to the names that had existed. The reason for this is that the possible state is persuasive: what has not yet been, we do not believe can be; but as for what has already been found, if it had existed, it cannot not be.
# literal_translation = From account-of that in art-of the-praise they-were holding to-the-names which were; and-the-reason in this, it [is] that the-state the-possible it [is] persuasive; and-which not was yet, so-not-are-we believing that-it is-possible that it-be; and-as-for which indeed was is-found, if was indeed was existent, so-not is-possible that-not it-be.
