# text = ومن قبل ان تركب المديح ينبغى ان يكون غير بسيط بل مزوج وان يكون هذا من اشيا مخوفة محزنة [حرقه مملوه حزنا] وان يكون محاكى لهذه اذ كان هذا هو خاصة المحاكاة لمثل هذه فهو ظاهر اولا انه ليس يسهل ولا على الرجال الانجاد ان تروى دايما فى التغير من الفلاح الى لافلاح وذلك ان هذا ليس هو مخوف ولا صعب لكن لهذه الى دٯلها
# transliteration = wa-min qibali anna tarakkuba l-madīḥi yanbaghī an yakūna ghayra basīṭin bal muzawwajan wa-an yakūna hādhā min ashyāʾa makhūfatin muḥzinatin [ḥurqatin mamlūʾatin ḥuznan] wa-an yakūna muḥākiyan li-hādhihi idh kāna hādhā huwa khāṣṣata l-muḥākāti li-mithli hādhihi fa-huwa ẓāhirun awwalan annahū laysa yashulu wa-lā ʿalā l-rijāli l-anjādi an turwā dāʾiman fī l-taghayyuri mina l-falāḥi ilā lā falāḥin wa-dhālika anna hādhā laysa huwa makhūfan wa-lā ṣaʿban lākin li-hādhihi ilā dqlhā (?)
# prose_translation = And because the composition of praise ought to be not simple but coupled, and this [made] of fearful and grievous things [a burning filled with grief], and imitative of these, since this is what is proper to the imitation of such things, it is evident, first, that it is not easy, not even for noble men, to be related as always in the change from success to non-success; for this is neither fearful nor hard, but belongs to these … (?).
# literal_translation = And-from account-of that composition-of the-praise it-is-fitting that it-be other-than simple but coupled, and-that be this from things fearful grievous [a-burning filled grief], and-that it-be imitating to-these, since was this it property-of the-imitation to-like-of these; so-it [is] evident firstly that-it not is-easy, and-not upon the-men the-noble, that they-be-related always in the-change from the-success to non-success; and-that [is] that this is-not it fearful and-not hard, but to-these to ?(undotted).
