# sent_id = 13.4
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 13.4
# translation_lang = en
# text = ولا ايضا هى مخوفة ولا ايضا هى للذين هم ارديا جدا من فلاح الى لافلاح ان يسقطون وذلك ان التى لمحبة الانسانية فلها قوام مثل هذا ولا ايضا الحزن *الـ*وف ايضا ***ك انه اما ذاك هو الى من لا يستحق عند ما لا يصلح واما هذا ڡالٮى من يشتبهه اخر اما هذا الى من لا يستحق واما الخوف فالى من الشبيه فاذا ما يعرض ليس هو لا للخوف ولا للحزن
# transliteration = wa-lā ayḍan hiya makhūfatun wa-lā ayḍan hiya li-lladhīna hum ardiyāʾu jiddan min falāḥin ilā lā falāḥin an yasquṭūna wa-dhālika anna allatī li-maḥabbati l-insāniyyati fa-lahā qiwāmun mithlu hādhā wa-lā ayḍan al-ḥuznu wa-l-khawfu (?) ayḍan wa-dhālika (?) annahū ammā dhāka huwa ilā man lā yastaḥiqqu ʿinda mā lā yaṣluḥu wa-ammā hādhā fa-ilā man yashtabihuhū ākharu ammā hādhā ilā man lā yastaḥiqqu wa-ammā l-khawfu fa-ilā man al-shabīhu fa-idhan mā yaʿriḍu laysa huwa lā li-l-khawfi wa-lā li-l-ḥuzni
# prose_translation = Nor again is it fearful; nor is it [the case], for those who are very bad, that they fall from success to non-success. For what belongs to love of humanity has a structure of this kind, but not grief, and not fear (?) either. That (?) is because the former is toward one who does not deserve [it], when he does not fare well, while the latter is toward one whom another resembles: this [grief] toward one who does not deserve, and fear toward one who is alike. So what happens is then neither for fear nor for grief.
# literal_translation = And-not also it [is] fearful; and-not also it [is] for-those-who they [are] bad very, from success to non-success, that they-fall; and-that [is] that which [is] for-love-of the-humanity, so-to-it [is] structure like this, and-not also the-grief, and-the-fear(?) also; and-that(?) [is] that-it as-for that-one it [is] toward whom not deserves when not he-fares-well, and-as-for this so-toward whom resembles-him another; as-for this toward whom not deserves, and-as-for the-fear so-toward whom [is] the-like; so-then what happens is-not it neither for-the-fear nor for-the-grief.
