# sent_id = 13.5
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 13.5
# translation_lang = en
# text = فبقى اذا المتوسط بين هذين هو هذا اعنى الذى لا فرق فيه لا فى الفضيلة والعدل ولا ايضا يميل الى لافلاح ولانجح بسبب الجور والتعب بل بسبب خطا ما وذلك الذين هم فى جلالة عظيمة وفى نجاح وفلاح بمنزلة اوديفوس وثواسطس وهولا الذين هم من قبل هذه الاحساب ومشهورين
# transliteration = fa-baqiya idhan al-mutawassiṭu bayna hādhayni huwa hādhā aʿnī alladhī lā farqa fīhi lā fī l-faḍīlati wa-l-ʿadli wa-lā ayḍan yamīlu ilā lā falāḥin wa-lā najḥin bi-sababi l-jawri wa-l-taʿabi bal bi-sababi khaṭaʾin mā wa-dhālika alladhīna hum fī jalālatin ʿaẓīmatin wa-fī najāḥin wa-falāḥin bi-manzilati Ūdīfūs wa-Thuwāsṭus wa-hāʾulāʾi alladhīna hum min qibali hādhihi l-aḥsābi wa-mashhūrīna
# prose_translation = What remains, then, is the one intermediate between these two, and he is this: I mean the one in whom there is no distinction, neither in virtue nor in justice, and who again does not incline to non-success and non-prosperity because of injustice and toil, but because of some error; that is, those who are in great glory and in prosperity and success, like Oedipus and Thyestes, and those who are of such lineages, and famous.
# literal_translation = So-remained then the-intermediate between these-two; it [is] this, I-mean the-one-who no difference in-him, neither in the-virtue and-the-justice, and-not also inclines to non-success and-non-prosperity by-cause-of the-injustice and-the-toil, but by-cause-of error some; and-that [is] those-who they [are] in glory great and-in prosperity and-success, in-the-rank-of Oedipus and-Thyestes, and-these who they [are] from the-side-of these the-lineages, and-famous.
