# translation_lang = en
# text = والدليل على ذلك ما يكون واولا كانوا يحصون الخرافات الذين يوجدون لكميا يطنون واما الان فقد تركب المديحات قليلا عند البيوت مثل ما كان بسبب القامان واوديفوس واورسطس ومالاغرس وثواسطس وطيلافس وساير القوم الاخر كم كان مبلغهم ممن مرت به مصايب ونابته النوايب ان ينفعلوا ويفعلوا اشيا صعبة
# transliteration = wa-l-dalīlu ʿalā dhālika mā yakūnu wa-awwalan kānū yuḥṣūna l-khurāfāti alladhīna yūjadūna lkmyā (?) yaẓunnūna (?) wa-ammā l-āna fa-qad turakkabu l-madīḥātu qalīlan ʿinda l-buyūti mithla mā kāna bi-sababi l-Qāmān wa-Ūdīfūs wa-Ūrasṭus wa-Mālāghrus wa-Thuwāsṭus wa-Ṭīlāfus wa-sāʾiri l-qawmi l-ākhari kam kāna mablaghuhum mimman marrat bihī maṣāʾibu wa-nābathu l-nawāʾibu an yanfaʿilū wa-yafʿalū ashyāʾa ṣaʿbatan
# prose_translation = The proof of this is what happens. At first they used to enumerate the tales that were found … (?) they think (?); but now praises are composed sparingly, about the houses, such as what happened on account of Alcmaeon, Oedipus, Orestes, Meleager, Thyestes, Telephus and the rest of the other people, however many they were, of those through whom calamities passed and whom misfortunes befell, [namely] that they should suffer and do hard things.
# literal_translation = And-the-proof of that [is] what happens: and-firstly they-were counting the-tales which are-found ?(lkmyā) they-think(?); and-as-for now so-indeed are-composed the-praises little at the-houses, like what was by-cause-of Alcmaeon and-Oedipus and-Orestes and-Meleager and-Thyestes and-Telephus and-rest-of the-people the-other, how-many was their-amount, of-whom passed by-him calamities and-befell-him the-misfortunes, that they-suffer and-do things hard.
