# text = ولذلك قد يخطى الذين يلزمون اوريفيدس اللوم من قبل انه جعل مدايحه على هذا الضرب وذلك ان كثيرا مما يوول بالامر الى لافلاح ولانجاح والى شقا البخوت وذلك كما قلنا مما هو مستقيم
# transliteration = wa-li-dhālika qad yukhṭiʾu alladhīna yulzimūna Ūrīfīdis al-lawma min qibali annahū jaʿala madāʾiḥahū ʿalā hādhā l-ḍarbi wa-dhālika anna kathīran mimmā yaʾūlu bi-l-amri ilā lā falāḥin wa-lā najāḥin wa-ilā shaqāʾi l-bukhūti wa-dhālika kamā qulnā mimmā huwa mustaqīmun
# prose_translation = Therefore those who lay blame on Euripides because he made his praises in this manner are in error; for many [of them] are of the kind that brings the matter to non-success and non-prosperity and to wretchedness of fortunes, and that, as we have said, is among what is correct.
# literal_translation = And-for-that indeed err those-who impose-on Euripides the-blame from account-of that-he made his-praises upon this the-manner; and-that [is] that many [are] of-what leads with-the-matter to non-success and-non-prosperity and-to misery-of the-fortunes; and-that, as we-said, [is] of-what it [is] correct.
