# text = واعظم الدلايل على ذلك ان هذه الاشيا التى تكون من الجهادات ومن المسكن ترى بهذه الحال غير ان هولا يصلحون الخطا وان كان اوريفيدس دبر هذه الاشيا تدبيرا حسنا الا انه قد يرى انه ادخل فى باب المدايح من الشعرا الاخر
# transliteration = wa-aʿẓamu l-dalāʾili ʿalā dhālika anna hādhihi l-ashyāʾa allatī takūnu mina l-jihādāti wa-mina l-maskani turā bi-hādhihi l-ḥāli ghayra anna hāʾulāʾi yuṣliḥūna l-khaṭaʾa wa-in kāna Ūrīfīdis dabbara hādhihi l-ashyāʾa tadbīran ḥasanan illā annahū qad yurā annahū adkhalu fī bābi l-madāʾiḥi mina l-shuʿarāʾi l-ukhari
# prose_translation = The greatest proof of this is that these things which come about in the contests and in the dwelling are seen in this condition, except that these [poets] correct the error; and even if Euripides managed these things well, yet he is seen to have entered further into the domain of praises than the other poets.
# literal_translation = And-greatest-of the-proofs of that [is] that these the-things which are from the-contests and-from the-dwelling are-seen in-this the-state, except that these correct the-error; and-if was Euripides managed these the-things a-managing good, yet that-it indeed is-seen that-he [is] more-entering in chapter-of the-praises than the-poets the-other.
