# text = وليس هذه هى اللذة من صناعة المديح لكنها اكثر مناسبة لصناعة الهجا وذلك ان هنالك فالاعدا والمبغضون هم الذين يوجدون فى الخرافة بمنزلة اوسطس والسطس اللذين عند ما صارا اصدقا فى اخر الامر قد تبديا وڡعال فيهما فى القينة امر الميتة لا واحد من رفيقه وقرينه
# transliteration = wa-laysa hādhihi hiya l-ladhdhata min ṣināʿati l-madīḥi lākinnahā aktharu munāsabatan li-ṣināʿati l-hijāʾi wa-dhālika anna hunālika fa-l-aʿdāʾu wa-l-mubghiḍūna hum alladhīna yūjadūna fī l-khurāfati bi-manzilati Ūsṭus wa-Alsṭus alladhayni ʿinda mā ṣārā aṣdiqāʾa fī ākhiri l-amri qad tabaddayā wa-fʿāl (?) fīhimā fī l-qaynati amru l-mītati lā wāḥidun min rafīqihī wa-qarīnihī
# prose_translation = This is not the pleasure that comes from the art of praise; rather it is more suited to the art of lampoon. For there the enemies and those who hate are the ones found in the tale, like Orestes (?) and Aegisthus (?), the two who, when they became friends at the end of the affair, came out, and … (?) in them, in the play (?), the matter of death: not one [dies] at the hand of his companion and associate.
# literal_translation = And-is-not this it the-pleasure from art-of the-praise, but-it [is] more suitability to-art-of the-lampoon; and-that [is] that there so-the-enemies and-the-haters, they [are] those-who are-found in the-tale, in-the-rank-of Orestes(?) and-Aegisthus(?), the-two-who when became friends in end-of the-matter indeed came-out, and-?(undotted) in-them in the-play(?) matter-of the-death, not one from his-companion and-his-associate.
