# text = فاما كون الذى للخوف والحزن فانما يحصل من البصر وقد يوجد شى ما من قوام الامور ما هو منذ قديم الدهر وهو لشاعر حاذق
# transliteration = fa-ammā kawnu alladhī li-l-khawfi wa-l-ḥuzni fa-innamā yaḥṣulu mina l-baṣari wa-qad yūjadu shayʾun mā min qiwāmi l-umūri mā huwa mundhu qadīmi l-dahri wa-huwa li-shāʿirin ḥādhiqin
# prose_translation = As for the arising of what belongs to fear and grief, it comes about only from sight; yet something is also found from the structure of the events, which is from ancient time, and it belongs to a skilled poet.
# literal_translation = So-as-for being-of that-which [is] for-the-fear and-the-grief, so-only it-comes-about from the-sight; and-indeed is-found thing some from structure-of the-things, what it [is] since ancient-of the-time, and-it [is] for-poet skilled.
