# transliteration = wa-hiya an naʾkhudha ayyumā hiya l-ashyāʾu ghayru l-ṣaʿbati mina l-nawāʾibi allatī tanūbu wa-ayyumā hiya allatī turā annahā yasīratun wa-dhālika annahū qad yajibu ḍarūratan an yakūna mithlu hādhihi l-afʿāli l-irādiyyati immā li-l-aṣdiqāʾi baʿḍihim ilā baʿḍin wa-immā li-l-aʿdāʾi wa-immā lā li-hāʾulāʾi wa-lā li-hāʾulāʾi
# prose_translation = Namely, that we take which of the misfortunes that befall are the things that are not hard, and which are those that are seen to be slight. For such voluntary actions must necessarily be either between friends, one toward another, or between enemies, or neither between these nor between those.
# literal_translation = And-it [is] that we-take which they [are] the-things other-than the-hard of the-misfortunes which befall, and-which they [are] those-which are-seen that-they [are] slight; and-that [is] that-it indeed is-necessary necessarily that be like-of these the-actions the-voluntary either for-the-friends some-of-them to some, or for-the-enemies, or neither for-these nor for-these.
