# transliteration = wa-ammā matā ikhtāra (?) l-taʾthīrāti wa-l-ālāma fī l-maḥabbāti [wa-l-muḥibbīna] bi-manzilati immā an yakūna akhun yaqtulu l-akha wa-bnun li-l-ābāʾi (?) wa-ummun li-bnihā aw ibnun li-ummihī aw kāna muzmiʿan an yafʿala shayʾan ākhara min mithli hādhihi fa-qad yuḥtāju fī mithli dhālika ilā hādhihi l-khallati
# prose_translation = But when [the poet] chooses (?) the affections and pains within friendships [and lovers], as when either a brother kills his brother, or a son his father (?), or a mother her son, or a son his mother, or is about to do some other such thing, then in such a case this quality is needed.
