# text = وهو ان يكون الخرافات التى قد اخذت على هذه لا تحل وتبطل واعنى بذلك مثل انه ليس لاحد يبطل من امر المراة المعروفة باقلوطميسطر انه لم ينلها الميتة من اورسطس ولا للمعروفة بااريفيلى من القيماون
# transliteration = wa-huwa an yakūna l-khurāfātu allatī qad ukhidhat ʿalā hādhihi lā tuḥallu wa-tubṭalu wa-aʿnī bi-dhālika mithla annahū laysa li-aḥadin yubṭilu min amri l-marʾati l-maʿrūfati bi-Aqlūṭamīsṭar annahū lam yanalhā l-mītatu min Ūrasṭus wa-lā li-l-maʿrūfati bi-Aarīfīlī mina l-Qīmāwun
# prose_translation = Namely, that the tales which have been received on these [terms] are not to be undone and nullified. By that I mean, for example, that no one may nullify, in the matter of the woman known as Clytemnestra, [the fact] that death did not come to her from Orestes, nor [may one do so] for the woman known as Eriphyle, from Alcmaeon.
# literal_translation = And-it [is] that be the-tales which indeed were-taken upon these not are-undone and-are-nullified; and-I-mean by-that like that-it is-not for-anyone [he-]nullifies from matter-of the-woman the-known as-Clytemnestra that-it not reached-her the-death from Orestes, and-not for-the-known as-Eriphyle from Alcmaeon.
