# sent_id = 14.13
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 14.13
# translation_lang = en
# text = واما معنى الا يفعل بالارادة عند ما يعرفون وان يفعلوا من حيث لا يعرفون ثم يعرفون المحبة والصادقة خيرا فهو حال ردية وهذا كحال سوقفلس واوديفس فهذه هى خارجة عن القينة نفسها واما ما هو فى المديح فبمنزلة القاماون واسطودامنطس او حٮٮ ٮقول على نحو الضربة لاودوسيس
# transliteration = wa-ammā maʿnā allā yafʿala bi-l-irādati ʿinda mā yaʿrifūna wa-an yafʿalū min ḥaythu lā yaʿrifūna thumma yaʿrifūna l-maḥabbata wa-l-ṣādiqata akhīran fa-huwa ḥālun radīʾatun wa-hādhā ka-ḥāli Sūqaflus wa-Ūdīfus fa-hādhihi hiya khārijatun ʿani l-qaynati nafsihā wa-ammā mā huwa fī l-madīḥi fa-bi-manzilati l-Qāmāwun wa-Asṭūdāmanṭus aw ḥīna (?) yaqūlu (?) ʿalā naḥwi l-ḍarbati li-Ūdūsīs
# prose_translation = As for the meaning of not acting voluntarily while they know, and of their acting without knowing and afterwards recognizing the love and the true [bond], that is a bad state; this is like the case of Sophocles and Oedipus. These lie outside the play (?) itself. As for what is in praise, it is like Alcmaeon and Astydamas, or when (?) he speaks (?) of the manner of the blow to Odysseus.
# literal_translation = And-as-for meaning-of that-not he-does by-the-will when they-know, and-that they-do from where not they-know, then they-know the-love and-the-true later(?), so-it [is] state bad; and-this [is] like-state-of Sophocles and-Oedipus; so-these they [are] outside from the-play(?) itself; and-as-for what it [is] in the-praise, so-in-the-rank-of Alcmaeon and-Astydamas, or when(?) he-says(?) upon manner-of the-blow to-Odysseus.
