# sent_id = 14.16
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 14.16
# translation_lang = en
# text = فمن كان من هولا يعرف وهو ٮعى ولا يفعل فهو ارذل وذلك ان نشيده حينيذ هو شنع كريه وليس هو داخلا فى باب المدح من قبل انه قد كان اعتبر ولذلك ليس انسان ان يفعل على جهة التشابه الا اقل ذاك بمنزلة ما ٮاٮ طىعوٮى لقريو يمن
# transliteration = fa-man kāna min hāʾulāʾi yaʿrifu wa-huwa yabghī (?) wa-lā yafʿalu fa-huwa ardhalu wa-dhālika anna nashīdahū ḥīnaʾidhin huwa shaniʿun karīhun wa-laysa huwa dākhilan fī bābi l-madḥi min qibali annahū qad kāna iʿtabara wa-li-dhālika laysa insānun an yafʿala ʿalā jihati l-tashābuhi illā aqalla dhāka bi-manzilati mā ?ā? (?) ṭīʿū?ī (?) li-Qaryū Yamun
# prose_translation = Whoever of these knows, and wants (?) [to act], and does not act, is the basest; for his song is then ugly and detestable, and it does not enter into the domain of praise, because he had considered (?) [it]. For that reason there is no one who acts in the manner of likeness except very rarely, as in … (Antigone?): to Creon, Haemon.
# literal_translation = So-who was of these knows and-he wants(?) and-not does, so-he [is] basest; and-that [is] that his-song then it [is] ugly detestable, and-is-not it entering in chapter-of the-praise, from account-of that-he indeed had considered; and-for-that not-is man that he-does upon manner-of the-likeness except least-of that, in-the-rank-of what ?(undotted) ?(Antigone?) to-Creon Haemon.
