# translation_lang = en
# text = والخير لمن هو غير عارف بان يفعل ان يكون اذا فعل ان يتعرف وذلك ان الكراهة حينيذ والشناعة لا يدانيانه واما الاستدلال والتعرف فهو اعجب [واجود]
# transliteration = wa-l-khayru li-man huwa ghayru ʿārifin bi-an yafʿala an yakūna idhā faʿala an yataʿarrafa wa-dhālika anna l-karāhata ḥīnaʾidhin wa-l-shanāʿata lā yudāniyānihī wa-ammā l-istidlālu wa-l-taʿarrufu fa-huwa aʿjabu [wa-ajwadu]
# prose_translation = Better, for one who does not know that he is acting, is that, when he has acted, he should come to recognize; for then repugnance and ugliness do not come near him, while recognition and acknowledgement are more astonishing [and better].
# literal_translation = And-the-good for-whom he [is] other-than knowing to-that he-does, [is] that it-be, when he-did, that he-recognizes; and-that [is] that the-repugnance then and-the-ugliness not they-two-approach-him; and-as-for the-recognition and-the-acknowledgement, so-it [is] more-wondrous [and-better].
