# text = ومن البين ان اواخر الخرافات انما ينبغى ان تعرض لها وتنوبها من العادة نفسها وليس كحال فيما كان من الحيلة عند ميديا وكما كان مما كان الى اٮٮلس من انقلاب المراكب [لا للغرق]
# transliteration = wa-mina l-bayyini anna awākhira l-khurāfāti innamā yanbaghī an taʿriḍa lahā wa-tanūbahā mina l-ʿādati nafsihā wa-laysa ka-ḥāli fīmā kāna mina l-ḥīlati ʿinda Mīdiyā wa-kamā kāna mimmā kāna ilā Īlis(?) min inqilābi l-marākibi [lā li-l-gharaqi]
# prose_translation = It is evident that the endings of the tales ought to befall and overtake them only from the habit itself, and not as in the case of the contrivance there was in Medea, and as with what happened at Īlis (?) from the overturning of the ships [not for drowning].
# literal_translation = And-of the-evident [is] that endings-of the-tales only it-is-fitting that befall to-them and-overtake-them from the-habit itself, and-is-not like-case-of in-what was of the-contrivance at Medea, and-as was of-what was to Īlis(?) from overturning-of the-ships [not for-the-drowning].
