# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 15.11
# translation_lang = en
# text = والتشبيه والماحكاة هى مدايح الاشيا التى هى فى غاية الفضيلة او كما يجب ان سٮهوا المصورون الحذاق الجياد وذلك ان هولا باجمعهم عند ما ياتون بصورهم وخلقهم من حيث يشبهون ياتون بالرسوم جيادا كذلك الشاعر ايضا عند ما يشبه الغضابى والكسالى ياتى هذه الاشيا الاخر التى توجد لهم فى عاداتهم فعلى هذا ينبغى للحذاق ان ياتوا بمثال الصعوبة بمنزلة ما اجاں اوميرس من خبر اخيلوس
# transliteration = wa-l-tashbīhu wa-l-māḥakātu hiya madāʾiḥu l-ashyāʾi allatī hiya fī ghāyati l-faḍīlati aw kamā yajibu an shabbahū(?) al-muṣawwirūna l-ḥudhdhāqu l-jiyādu wa-dhālika anna hāʾulāʾi bi-ajmaʿihim ʿinda mā yaʾtūna bi-ṣuwarihim wa-khalqihim min ḥaythu yushabbihūna yaʾtūna bi-l-rusūmi jiyādan kadhālika l-shāʿiru ayḍan ʿinda mā yushabbihu l-ghaḍābā wa-l-kasālā yaʾtī hādhihi l-ashyāʾa l-ukhara allatī tūjadu lahum fī ʿādātihim fa-ʿalā hādhā yanbaghī li-l-ḥudhdhāqi an yaʾtū bi-mithāli l-ṣuʿūbati bi-manzilati mā ajā(?) Ūmīrus min khabari Akhīlūs
# prose_translation = Likening and imitation are praises of things at the utmost of virtue, or as the skilled, good painters must have likened (?); for all of these, when they render their forms and shapes, insofar as they make likenesses, render the drawings good. So too the poet, when he likens the irascible and the lazy, brings these other things that are found in them in their habits. Accordingly the skilled ought to bring an example of harshness, as Homer […] (?) in the account of Achilles.
# literal_translation = And-the-likening and-the-imitation, they [are] praises-of the-things which they [are] in utmost-of the-virtue, or as it-is-necessary that likened(?) the-painters the-skilled the-good; and-that [is] that these with-all-of-them, when they-bring with-their-forms and-their-shapes, from where they-liken, they-bring with-the-drawings good; likewise the-poet also, when he-likens the-irascible and-the-lazy, brings these the-things the-other which are-found for-them in their-habits; so-upon this it-is-fitting for-the-skilled that they-bring with-example-of the-harshness, like what […](?) Homer of account-of Achilles.
