# transliteration = wa-dhālika anna minhā mā huwa fī amri l-taṣdīqi akthara fī bābi l-ṣināʿati wa-jamīʿu hādhihi allatī hiya amthāluhā wa-minhā mā yūjadu fīhā l-idāratu wa-l-taqlību akthara mithla anna hādhihi allatī takūnu bi-l-taghassuli ajwadu
# prose_translation = For among them there are some that are more in the matter of assent, within the domain of art, and all those that are like them; and among them there are some in which reversal and turning are found more, as [in the fact] that those that come about through the washing are better.
# literal_translation = And-that [is] that of-them [is] what it [is] in matter-of the-assent more, in chapter-of the-art, and-all these which they [are] their-likes; and-of-them [is] what is-found in-it the-turning and-the-reversal more, like that these which are by-the-washing [are] better.
