# text = والثوانى التى علمها الشاعر لهذا السبب بلا صناعة مثل جانب المعروفة بباغانيا وهو الذى به استدلت اباغانيا انه ارسطس وذلك انه اما تلك فبالرسالة الى ذاك واما هذا فيخبر بما يريده الشاعر لا الخرافة وحكاية الحديث
# transliteration = wa-l-thawānī allatī ʿalimahā l-shāʿiru li-hādhā l-sababi bi-lā ṣināʿatin mithla jānibi l-maʿrūfati bi-Bāghāniyā wa-huwa alladhī bihī istadallat Abāghāniyā annahū Arisṭus wa-dhālika annahū ammā tilka fa-bi-l-risālati ilā dhāka wa-ammā hādhā fa-yukhbiru bi-mā yurīduhū l-shāʿiru lā l-khurāfatu wa-ḥikāyatu l-ḥadīthi
# prose_translation = The second are those which the poet knew (made?), and for this reason they are without art, such as the part of the [play] known as Iphigenia; it is that by which Iphigenia inferred that he was Orestes. For she [recognized] by the letter to that one, while this one reports what the poet wants, not the tale and the narration of the story.
# literal_translation = And-the-second-ones which knew(made?)-them the-poet [are] for-this the-reason with-no art, like part-of the-known as-Iphigenia; and-it [is] that-which by-it inferred Iphigenia that-he [is] Orestes; and-that [is] that-it, as-for that-one, so-by-the-letter to that-one, and-as-for this-one, so-he-reports with-what wants-it the-poet, not the-tale and-narration-of the-story.
