# text = والثالث هو ان يكون ينال الانسان ان يحس عند ما يرى كالحال فيما كان باهل ديقوغانس فى قبرس فانه قال انه لما راى الكتابات بكا وكذلك امر اهل القينس من القول فانه لما سمع العواد وتذكر دمع ومن هنالك عرف بعضهم بعضا
# transliteration = wa-l-thālithu huwa an yakūna yanālu l-insāna an yuḥissa ʿinda mā yarā ka-l-ḥāli fīmā kāna bi-ahli Dīqūghānis fī Qubrus fa-innahū qāla annahū lammā raʾā l-kitābāti bakā wa-kadhālika amru ahli l-Qīnis mina l-qawli fa-innahū lammā samiʿa l-ʿawwāda wa-tadhakkara damaʿa wa-min hunālika ʿarafa baʿḍuhum baʿḍan
# prose_translation = The third is that it befalls a man to perceive when he sees, as in the case of what happened with the people of Dicaeogenes in Cyprus: he said that when he saw the writings he wept. Likewise the affair of the people of Alcinous, from the speech: when he heard the lute-player and remembered, he shed tears; and from there they recognized one another.
# literal_translation = And-the-third, it [is] that be befalls the-man that he-perceive when he-sees, like-the-case in-what was with-people-of Dicaeogenes in Cyprus: so-verily-he said that-he when he-saw the-writings wept; and-likewise [is] affair-of people-of Alcinous from the-speech: so-verily-he when he-heard the-lute-player and-remembered shed-tears; and-from there knew some-of-them some.
