# sent_id = 16.10
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 16.10
# translation_lang = en
# text = وقد يوجد ضرب اخر ايضا مركب الماخوذ من مغالطة القياس التى لثااطرن بمنزلة فيما دون من امر اودوسيا ذلك المبشر الطاهر وذلك ان من القوس زعم انه ليس يمكن انسان اخر فقد قال ذلك الشاعر والخير ايضا الذى اتى فى ذلك قد خبر فيه في امر القوس ليعرف ما لم يروا ما القول انه بتوسط ذاك كاٮٮ ٮعرف ففى هذا كانت المغالطة فى القياس
# transliteration = wa-qad yūjadu ḍarbun ākharu ayḍan murakkabun al-maʾkhūdhu min mughālaṭati l-qiyāsi allatī li-thāʾāṭrun bi-manzilati fīmā duwwina min amri Ūdūsiyā dhālika l-mubashshiri l-ṭāhiri wa-dhālika anna mina l-qawsi zaʿama annahū laysa yumkinu insānun ākharu fa-qad qāla dhālika l-shāʿiru wa-l-khayru ayḍan alladhī atā fī dhālika qad khubbira fīhi fī amri l-qawsi li-yaʿrifa mā lam yaraw mā l-qawlu annahū bi-tawassuṭi dhāka kānat(?) taʿrifu(?) fa-fī hādhā kānati l-mughālaṭatu fī l-qiyāsi
# prose_translation = There is also another, composite kind, taken from the fallacy of reasoning that belongs to the theatre, as in what was recorded about Odysseus, that pure (?) herald. For about the bow he claimed that no other man could [do it]; so that poet said. And the good (report?) too that came in that: it was reported in it, about the bow, that he would recognize what they had not seen. What is the statement that through that one she would recognize (?)? In this lay the fallacy in reasoning.
# literal_translation = And-indeed is-found kind other also composite, the-taken from fallacy-of the-reasoning which [is] for-the-theatre, like in-what was-recorded of affair-of Odysseus, that the-herald the-pure; and-that [is] that of the-bow he-claimed that-it not is-possible man other; so-indeed said that the-poet; and-the-good(report?) also which came in that, indeed it-was-reported in-it in affair-of the-bow, so-that he-know what not they-saw; what [is] the-statement that-it by-mediation-of that-one was(?) recognizes(?); so-in this was the-fallacy in the-reasoning.
