# sent_id = 16.11
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 16.11
# translation_lang = en
# text = غير ان الاستدلال الفاضل على كل شى فهى الماخوذة من امور الفعل الارادى ولذلك مثل هذا ارى سوفقلس فى اوديفس وفى ايباغانيا ايضا وذلك انه قد كان يريد على الحقيقة ان يدون فى ذلك كلام وذلك ان هذه الامور هى وحدها فقط بلا اشيا معمولة وبلا اشيا فى العنق
# transliteration = ghayra anna l-istidlāla l-fāḍila ʿalā kulli shayʾin fa-hiya l-maʾkhūdhatu min umūri l-fiʿli l-irādiyyi wa-li-dhālika mithla hādhā arā Sūfuqlis fī Ūdīfus wa-fī Ībāghāniyā ayḍan wa-dhālika annahū qad kāna yurīdu ʿalā l-ḥaqīqati an yudawwana fī dhālika kalāmun wa-dhālika anna hādhihi l-umūra hiya waḥdahā faqaṭ bi-lā ashyāʾa maʿmūlatin wa-bi-lā ashyāʾa fī l-ʿunuqi
# prose_translation = Yet the recognition that excels above everything is the one taken from matters of voluntary action; for that reason Sophocles showed the like of this in Oedipus, and in Iphigenia too, for he truly wanted words to be recorded in that. For these matters alone are without made things and without things on the neck.
# literal_translation = Except that the-inference the-excellent upon every thing, so-it [is] the-taken from matters-of the-action the-voluntary; and-for-that like-of this showed Sophocles in Oedipus and-in Iphigenia also; and-that [is] that-he indeed was wants upon the-truth that be-recorded in that speech; and-that [is] that these the-matters, they [are] alone-them only with-no things made and-with-no things on the-neck.
