# newpar id = chapter-17
# sent_id = 17.1
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 17.1
# translation_lang = en
# text = وقد ينبغى ان تقوم الخرافات وتتمم بالمقولة من قبل ان الامور توضع امام العينين جدا وذلك انه على هذه الجهة عند ما برى الشاعر على ما عند الامور المعمولة انفسها وعند ما يصير هناك يجد الشى الاولى والاحرى والاجمل ولا يذهب عليه البتة المضاد لهذه
# transliteration = wa-qad yanbaghī an tuqawwama l-khurāfātu wa-tutammama bi-l-maqūlati min qibali anna l-umūra tūḍaʿu amāma l-ʿaynayni jiddan wa-dhālika annahū ʿalā hādhihi l-jihati ʿinda mā barā l-shāʿiru ʿalā mā ʿinda l-umūri l-maʿmūlati anfusihā wa-ʿinda mā yaṣīru hunāka yajidu l-shayʾa l-awlā wa-l-aḥrā wa-l-ajmala wa-lā yadhhabu ʿalayhi l-battata l-muḍāddu li-hādhihi
# prose_translation = The tales ought to be constructed and completed by diction, because the matters are set very much before the eyes; for in this way, when the poet shapes (sees?) [them] as they are with the enacted matters themselves, and when he comes to be there, he finds what is most fitting, most appropriate and finest, and what is contrary to these does not escape him at all.
# literal_translation = And-indeed it-is-fitting that be-constructed the-tales and-be-completed by-the-diction, because that the-matters are-placed before the-two-eyes very; and-that [is] that-it upon this the-manner, when shaped(?) the-poet upon what [is] at the-matters the-done themselves, and-when he-becomes there, he-finds the-thing the-most-fitting and-the-most-appropriate and-the-finest, and-not escapes upon-him at-all the-contrary to-these.
