# sent_id = 18.9
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 18.9
# translation_lang = en
# text = هى ممتحنة مجربة فى كل شى وان لم يكن هكذى فهى لا محالة فى اشيا عظام وكٮيرة وانهم يتهمون وٮٯسمون الشعرا على جهة اخرى كما الان وذلك انه لما كان فى كل جزو وحيد شعرا جياد حداق هم يوهلون كل انسان لخيره الخاص
# transliteration = hiya mumtaḥanatun mujarrabatun fī kulli shayʾin wa-in lam yakun hākadhā fa-hiya lā maḥālata fī ashyāʾa ʿiẓāmin wa-kathīratin wa-innahum yattahimūna wa-yaqsimūna(?) l-shuʿarāʾa ʿalā jihatin ukhrā kamā l-āna wa-dhālika annahū lammā kāna fī kulli juzʾin waḥīdin shuʿarāʾu jiyādun ḥudhdhāqun hum yuʾahhilūna kulla insānin li-khayrihī l-khāṣṣi
# prose_translation = It is tested and tried in everything; and if it is not so, then it is without fail in great and many things. And they accuse and divide (?) the poets in another way, as now. That is because, since in every single part there were good, skilled poets, they deem every man worthy of his own particular good.
# literal_translation = It [is] tested tried in every thing; and-if not it-is thus, so-it [is], no avoiding, in things great and-many; and-verily-they accuse and-divide(?) the-poets upon manner other, as now; and-that [is] that-it, when was in every part single poets good skilled, they deem-worthy every man for-his-good the-particular.
