# prose_translation = As for the element, it is undivided; not all of it, but that of it from which the composite sound is by nature composed and comes to be. For the sounds of the beasts (?) are unarticulated, and not a single one of them is a composite sound; and not a single one of the parts of sounds is what I say belongs to the elements.
# literal_translation = So-as-for the-element, so-it [is] other-than divided, and-not-is all-of-it, but what was of-it from concern-of the-sound the-composite that it-be-composed and-come-to-be from-it; and-that [is] that sounds-of the-beasts(?) they [are] other-than articulated, and-not-is and-not one of-them sound composite; and-not-is and-not one of parts-of the-sounds what I-say that-it [is] for-the-elements.
