# sent_id = 20.3
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 20.3
# translation_lang = en
# text = واما هذا الصوت المركب فاجزاه جزوان اعنى المصوت ولا مصوت ونصف المصوت غير ان الصوت الذى يكون من غير القرع الكاين عند الشفتين او الاسنان هو صوت غير مفصل واما نصف الصوت الذى يكون مع القرع فليس له على انفراده صوت مسموع اذا ما حرك الس والر واما لا مصوت فهو الذى مع القرع اما على انفراده فليس له ولا صوت واحد مركب مسموع واما مع التى لها صوت مركب قد يكون مسموعا بمنزلة الى والد
# transliteration = wa-ammā hādhā l-ṣawtu l-murakkabu fa-ajzāʾuhū juzʾāni aʿnī l-muṣawwita wa-lā muṣawwitan wa-niṣfa l-muṣawwiti ghayra anna l-ṣawta alladhī yakūnu min ghayri l-qarʿi l-kāʾini ʿinda l-shafatayni awi l-asnāni huwa ṣawtun ghayru mufaṣṣalin wa-ammā niṣfu l-ṣawti alladhī yakūnu maʿa l-qarʿi fa-laysa lahū ʿalā infirādihī ṣawtun masmūʿun idhā mā ḥurrika l-s wa-l-r wa-ammā lā muṣawwitun fa-huwa alladhī maʿa l-qarʿi ammā ʿalā infirādihī fa-laysa lahū wa-lā ṣawtun wāḥidun murakkabun masmūʿun wa-ammā maʿa llatī lahā ṣawtun murakkabun qad yakūnu masmūʿan bi-manzilati l-y wa-l-d
# prose_translation = As for this composite sound, its parts are two, I mean the vowel, the non-vowel and the half-vowel. But the sound that comes about without the striking that occurs at the lips or the teeth is an unarticulated sound; and as for the half-sound that comes about with striking, it does not have by itself an audible sound, when s and r are moved. As for the non-vowel, it is the one that is with striking: by itself it has not even a single audible composite sound, but with those that have a composite sound it may become audible, such as y (?) and d.
# literal_translation = And-as-for this the-sound the-composite, so-its-parts [are] two-parts, I-mean the-vowel and-non-vowel and-half-of the-vowel; except that the-sound which is from without the-striking the-occurring at the-two-lips or the-teeth, it [is] sound other-than articulated; and-as-for half-of the-sound which is with the-striking, so-not-is to-it upon its-singleness sound audible, when are-moved the-s and-the-r; and-as-for non-vowel, so-it [is] which [is] with the-striking: as-for upon its-singleness, so-not-is to-it and-not sound one composite audible, and-as-for with which to-it [is] sound composite, indeed it-is audible, in-the-rank-of the-y and-the-d.
