# sent_id = 20.9
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 20.9
# translation_lang = en
# text = واما الكلمة فهى صوت دال او لفظة دالة تدل معما تدل عليه على الزمان جزو من اجزايه لا يدل على انفراده كما لا يدل جزو من اجزا الاسما على انفراده وذلك ان قولنا انسان او ابيض ليس يدلان على الزمان واما قولنا يمشى او مشى فقد يدلان على الزمان اما ذاك فعلى الزمان الحاضر واما هذا فعلى الزمان الماضى
# transliteration = wa-ammā l-kalimatu fa-hiya ṣawtun dāllun aw lafẓatun dāllatun tadullu maʿa mā tadullu ʿalayhi ʿalā l-zamāni juzʾun min ajzāʾihī lā yadullu ʿalā infirādihī kamā lā yadullu juzʾun min ajzāʾi l-asmāʾi ʿalā infirādihī wa-dhālika anna qawlanā insānun aw abyaḍu laysa yadullāni ʿalā l-zamāni wa-ammā qawlunā yamshī aw mashā fa-qad yadullāni ʿalā l-zamāni ammā dhāka fa-ʿalā l-zamāni l-ḥāḍiri wa-ammā hādhā fa-ʿalā l-zamāni l-māḍī
# prose_translation = As for the verb, it is a signifying sound or a signifying expression which, together with what it signifies, signifies time; no part of its parts signifies by itself, just as no part of the parts of nouns signifies by itself. For our saying "man" or "white" does not signify time, whereas our saying "walks" or "walked" does signify time: the former the present time, the latter the past time.
# literal_translation = And-as-for the-verb, so-it [is] sound signifying or expression signifying, it-signifies with what it-signifies upon-it upon the-time; part of its-parts not signifies upon its-singleness, as not signifies part of parts-of the-nouns upon its-singleness; and-that [is] that our-saying man or white not signify(dual) upon the-time, and-as-for our-saying walks or walked, so-indeed they-two-signify upon the-time: as-for that-one, so-upon the-time the-present, and-as-for this-one, so-upon the-time the-past.
