# translation_lang = en
# text = وليس كل قول مركب من الكلمة بمنزلة حد الانسان لكن قد يمكن ان يكون القول من كلم جزو من القول الدال على ما هو الشى بمنزلة ان يكون له بمنزلة قولنا قاللناس فى قولنا قاللناس يمشى
# transliteration = wa-laysa kullu qawlin murakkaban mina l-kalimati bi-manzilati ḥaddi l-insāni lākin qad yumkinu an yakūna l-qawlu min kalimin juzʾun mina l-qawli l-dālli ʿalā mā huwa l-shayʾu bi-manzilati an yakūna lahū bi-manzilati qawlinā qāllnās(?) fī qawlinā qāllnās(?) yamshī
# prose_translation = Not every statement is composed of the verb, for example the definition of man; but a statement may consist of words, a part of the statement signifying what the thing is, as in its having [such a part], as in our saying "qāllnās" (?) [Cleon] in our saying "qāllnās (?) walks".
# literal_translation = And-not-is every statement composed from the-verb, in-the-rank-of definition-of the-man; but indeed it-is-possible that be the-statement of words, part of the-statement the-signifying upon what it [is] the-thing, in-the-rank-of that there-be to-it, in-the-rank-of our-saying ? in our-saying ? walks.
