# text = والقول يكون واحدا على ضربين وذلك انه اما ان يكون القول واحدا بان يدل على واحد واما ان يكون واحدا برباطات كثيرة بمنزلة قولنا سفر او اوميروس هو المعروف بايلياس هو واحد وذلك ان هذا هو واحد برباط واما قولنا انسان يمشى فهو واحد من قبل انه يدل على واحد
# transliteration = wa-l-qawlu yakūnu wāḥidan ʿalā ḍarbayni wa-dhālika annahū immā an yakūna l-qawlu wāḥidan bi-an yadulla ʿalā wāḥidin wa-immā an yakūna wāḥidan bi-ribāṭātin kathīratin bi-manzilati qawlinā sifrun aw Ūmīrūs huwa l-maʿrūfu bi-Īliyās huwa wāḥidun wa-dhālika anna hādhā huwa wāḥidun bi-ribāṭin wa-ammā qawlunā insānun yamshī fa-huwa wāḥidun min qibali annahū yadullu ʿalā wāḥidin
# prose_translation = The statement is one in two ways: either the statement is one by signifying one thing, or it is one by many ligatures, as in our saying "The book (?) or Homer, the one known as the Iliad, is one", for this is one by a ligature; whereas our saying "man walks" is one because it signifies one thing.
# literal_translation = And-the-statement is one upon two-ways; and-that [is] that-it either that be the-statement one by-that it-signify upon one, or that it-be one by-ligatures many, in-the-rank-of our-saying: book or Homer, it [is] the-known by-Iliad, it [is] one; and-that [is] that this it [is] one by-ligature; and-as-for our-saying man walks, so-it [is] one from account-of that-it signifies upon one.
