# text = واعنى باللسان على انه لقوم اخر حتى يكون معلوم اللسان والحقيقى هما فى قوتهما شى واحد بعينه الا ان ذلك لقوم باعيانها وذلك ان سيغونن اما لاهل ٯوس فحقيقى واما لنا نحن فلسان واما دورو فهو لنا حقيقى واما لاهل فلسان
# transliteration = wa-aʿnī bi-l-lisāni ʿalā annahū li-qawmin ākhara ḥattā yakūna maʿlūman al-lisānu wa-l-ḥaqīqiyyu humā fī quwwatihimā shayʾun wāḥidun bi-ʿaynihī illā anna dhālika li-qawmin bi-aʿyānihā wa-dhālika anna sīghūnun ammā li-ahli Qūs(?) fa-ḥaqīqiyyun wa-ammā lanā naḥnu fa-lisānun wa-ammā dūrū fa-huwa lanā ḥaqīqiyyun wa-ammā li-ahli fa-lisānun
# prose_translation = By "tongue" I mean [a noun] in that it belongs to other people; so that it is known that the "tongue" and the proper [noun] are in their power one and the same thing, except that that [belongs] to particular peoples. For sīghūn is proper for the people of Qūs (?), while for us it is a "tongue"; and dūrū is proper for us, while for the people of […] it is a "tongue".
# literal_translation = And-I-mean by-the-tongue upon that-it [is] for-people other, so-that be known [that] the-tongue and-the-proper they-two [are] in their-power thing one in-itself, except that that [is] for-people in-their-selves; and-that [is] that sīghūn, as-for for-people-of Qūs so-proper, and-as-for for-us ourselves so-tongue; and-as-for dūrū so-it [is] for-us proper, and-as-for for-people-of so-tongue.
