# sent_id = 21.17
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 21.17
# translation_lang = en
# text = والاسم المعمول هو الاسم يضعه الساعه من غير ان يسميه صنف من الناس ٮا**ليه وقد يظن ان بعض الاسما هذه حالها فى كونها بمنزلة تلقيبه للقرون النابتة وتلقيبه لكاهن الذابح
# transliteration = wa-l-ismu l-maʿmūlu huwa l-ismu yaḍaʿuhū l-sāʿata min ghayri an yusammiyahū ṣinfun mina l-nāsi ?ā**līh wa-qad yuẓannu anna baʿḍa l-asmāʾi hādhihi ḥāluhā fī kawnihā bi-manzilati talqībihī li-l-qurūni l-nābitati wa-talqībihī li-kāhini l-dhābiḥi
# prose_translation = The made noun is the noun that [one] lays down on the spot (?), without any class of people naming it […]; and it is thought that some nouns are in this state, like his naming the horns "the sprouting ones" and his naming the priest "the slaughterer".
# literal_translation = And-the-noun the-made it [is] the-noun [that] he-lays-it-down the-hour, from other-than that names-it a-class of the-people ?; and-indeed is-thought that some-of the-nouns, this [is] their-state, in their-being in-manner-of his-naming for-the-horns the-sprouting and-his-naming for-priest the-slaughterer.
