# sent_id = 22.9
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 22.9
# translation_lang = en
# text = حتى يلزم ان ما يجرى من الهجا والٮلٮ [من الجرى] على هذا الضرب من الجدل ليس يجرى عل الاستقامة وعند يهزون بالشاعر بمنزلة اوقليدس ذلك الاول على انه قد كان يسهل عليه ان نفعل اعطا انسان هكذى كان يمد ما كان [يجد] يحب ويريد مده وكان يقصر حيث يريد وان يعمل الشعر المسمى ايانبوا بهذا اللفظ وهو قوله الذى زعم فيه اننى رايت ماراثون من حيث ٮسمى بالنعمة ولا ايضا كاكٮٮ اعٮدت ذاك
# transliteration = ḥattā yalzamu anna mā yajrī mina l-hijāʾi wa-l-thalbi(?) [mina l-jaryi] ʿalā hādhā l-ḍarbi mina l-jadali laysa yajrī ʿalā l-istiqāmati wa-ʿinda yahzaʾūna bi-l-shāʿiri bi-manzilati Ūqlīdis dhālika l-awwali ʿalā annahū qad kāna yashulu ʿalayhi an nafʿala iʿṭāʾa insānin hākadhā kāna yamuddu mā kāna [yajidu] yuḥibbu wa-yurīdu maddahū wa-kāna yuqaṣṣiru ḥaythu yurīdu wa-an yaʿmala l-shiʿra l-musammā īyānbū bi-hādhā l-lafẓi wa-huwa qawluhū alladhī zaʿama fīhi innanī raʾaytu Mārāthūn min ḥaythu ?smā(?) bi-l-niʿmati wa-lā ayḍan kāk??(?) aʿ?adtu(?) dhāka
# prose_translation = … so that it follows that the lampoon and censure (?) [of running] that is directed at this kind of discourse does not run straight — as when they mock the poet, like that ancient Euclides, on the ground that it had been easy for him that we (?) should do [so] by a man's granting (?): thus he used to lengthen whatever he liked and wished to lengthen, and to shorten where he wished; and to make the poetry called iambos in this very diction, namely his saying in which he claimed: "I saw Marathon, insofar as it is called (?) with grace (?)", and also not […] I […] that.
# literal_translation = So-that it-follows that what runs of the-lampoon and-the-censure [of the-running] upon this the-kind of the-dialectic not runs upon the-straightness; and-when they-mock at-the-poet, in-manner-of Euclides that the-first, upon that-it indeed was is-easy upon-him that we-do granting-of a-man: thus was he-lengthens what was [he-finds] he-likes and-wants its-lengthening, and-was he-shortens where he-wants; and-that he-make the-poetry the-named iambos with-this the-diction, and-it [is] his-saying which he-claimed in-it: that-I saw Marathon from where ? with-the-grace; and-not also ? I-? that.
