# sent_id = 22.13
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 22.13
# translation_lang = en
# text = والمقدار والتاديات وبانواع اخر فانه ان غير الاسما الحقيقية وقف على ان ما قلناه من ذلك حق مثل ان اوريفيدس واسخولس عند ما عملا الشعر المسمى ايانبوس فعلى هذا الفعل نفسه الا انه اذا ما نقل بدل الحقيقى من قبل انه قد اعتيد فى اللسان اما ذاك ***ا جيد شريف واما هذا فيرا مهين واسخولس عمل شعر فى فيلوقطيطس قال فيه ان السا* **لٮ لحومى ومششت رجلى فان فى هذا الكلام استعمل ووضع قوله مششت بدلا ***وله فاما الان انا من حيث على جهة الصغر والصغيرة بلا ان يصح يقول انسان من حيث **ر ڡدلك الحقيقة واما الان ڡلى انا من حيث اٮٮ صغيرا وٮسمى الضعيف والذى بلا منظر هذا الكلام ووصف المجلس دايما قاليون وقوله انه وضع بيدى انا الشفى مايدة صغيرة من حيث استعمل قوله ان انبا اليونانيين مايدة الصغيرة [صغير] بدل من اليونانين يسمون مايدة صغيرة
# transliteration = wa-l-miqdāru wa-l-taʾdiyātu wa-bi-anwāʿin ukhara fa-innahū in ghayyara l-asmāʾa l-ḥaqīqiyyata waqafa ʿalā anna mā qulnāhu min dhālika ḥaqqun mithla anna Ūrīfīdis wa-Askhūlus ʿinda mā ʿamilā l-shiʿra l-musammā īyānbūs fa-ʿalā hādhā l-fiʿli nafsihī illā annahū idhā mā nuqila badala l-ḥaqīqiyyi min qibali annahū qad uʿtīda fī l-lisāni ammā dhāka ***ā jayyidun sharīfun wa-ammā hādhā fa-yurā mahīnan wa-Askhūlus ʿamila shiʿran fī Fīlūqṭīṭis qāla fīhi inna l-sā* **l? luḥūmī wa-mashashtu rijlī fa-inna fī hādhā l-kalāmi istaʿmala wa-waḍaʿa qawlahū mashashtu badalan ***wlh fa-ammā l-āna anā min ḥaythu ʿalā jihati l-ṣighari wa-l-ṣaghīrati bi-lā an yaṣiḥḥa yaqūlu insānun min ḥaythu **r fdlk(?) al-ḥaqīqata wa-ammā l-āna flī(?) anā min ḥaythu a??(?) ṣaghīran wa-?smā(?) l-ḍaʿīfa wa-lladhī bi-lā manẓarin hādhā l-kalāmu wa-waṣfu l-majlisi dāʾiman qālyūn wa-qawluhū innahū waḍaʿa bi-yadī anā l-shafī māʾidatan ṣaghīratan min ḥaythu istaʿmala qawlahū inna anbāʾa l-yūnāniyyīna māʾidatu l-ṣaghīrati [ṣaghīrin] badalan mina l-yūnāniyyīna yusammūna māʾidatan ṣaghīratan
# prose_translation = As for measure, transferences and other kinds: if one changes the proper nouns, he will come to see that what we have said about this is true. For example, Euripides and Aeschylus, when both composed the poetry called iambos, [did] this same thing; except that when [a word] was transferred in place of the proper [word], because it had become customary in the "tongue", the one […] is good and noble, while the other is seen as mean. Aeschylus made a poem on Philoctetes, in which he said: "the […] […] my flesh, and I sucked (?) my foot"; and in this speech he used and put his word "I sucked (?)" in place of […]. As for "now I, in the manner of smallness and the small one", without its being correct (?), a man says, insofar as he […] (?) the proper [words]: "and now, then (?), I, insofar as […] small, and […] the weak and the one without looks". This is the speech; and the description of the seat "always qālyūn", and his saying that he placed by my hand — I, the wretched (?) — a small table, insofar as he used his saying that "the reports (?) of the Greeks: table of the small one" [small] in place of "the Greeks call a small table".
# literal_translation = And-the-measure and-the-transferences and-with-kinds other: so-verily-it, if he-changed the-nouns the-proper, he-came-upon that what we-said-it of that [is] true; like that Euripides and-Aeschylus, when they-two-made the-poetry the-named iambos, so-upon this the-doing itself; except that-it, whenever was-transferred instead-of the-proper, from account-of that-it indeed was-made-customary in the-tongue, as-for that-one ? good noble, and-as-for this-one so-is-seen mean. And-Aeschylus made poem on Philoctetes [in which] he-said in-it: that the-? ? my-flesh, and-I-sucked my-foot; so-verily in this the-speech he-used and-put his-saying "I-sucked" instead ?; so-as-for "now I, from where upon manner-of the-smallness and-the-small-one", with-no that it-be-correct says a-man, from where ? ? the-proper; and-as-for "now ?-for-me I from where ? small and-? the-weak and-the-one with-no look"; this the-speech; and-description-of the-seat "always qālyūn", and-his-saying that-he placed by-my-hand, I the-?wretched, table small, from where he-used his-saying that reports-of the-Greeks [are] table-of the-small-one [small] instead from the-Greeks [who] call table small.
