# sent_id = 22.14
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 22.14
# translation_lang = en
# text = وايضا كان يسمى المفسرين الحقيقيين ذوى المديح من حيث كان **بهم وزعم انهم كذلك لانهم يستعملون اشيا لا لم يقولها قط من الجدليين فى الجدل بمنزلة ما فى المجلس الذى من النحو لا امن الٮحلاٮ وبمنزلة القول القايل ان منك انت *ايضا قد كنت شى ما وبمنزلة القول القايل ان اخيلوس هو من اجل لا هو من اجل اخيلوس واشيا كثيرة من امثال هذه كم كانت
# transliteration = wa-ayḍan kāna yusammī l-mufassirīna l-ḥaqīqiyyīna dhawī l-madīḥi min ḥaythu kāna **bihim wa-zaʿama annahum kadhālika li-annahum yastaʿmilūna ashyāʾa lā lam yaqulhā qaṭṭu mina l-jadaliyyīna fī l-jadali bi-manzilati mā fī l-majlisi alladhī mina l-naḥwi lā amina l-?ḥlā?(?) wa-bi-manzilati l-qawli l-qāʾili inna minka anta *ayḍan qad kunta shayʾan mā wa-bi-manzilati l-qawli l-qāʾili inna Akhīlūs huwa min ajli lā huwa min ajli Akhīlūs wa-ashyāʾa kathīratin min amthāli hādhihi kam kānat
# prose_translation = Moreover, he used to call the true interpreters "people of praise", inasmuch as he […] them, and claimed that they are such because they use things that none of the dialecticians ever said in dialectic: for example, "what is in the hall, which is from the direction, not from the […]"; and the expression that says "from you, you, […] also, you were something"; and the expression that says "Achilles, he is for the sake of, not he is for the sake of Achilles"; and many things of the likes of these, however many they were.
# literal_translation = And-also was he-calls the-interpreters the-true possessors-of the-praise, from where was ?-them, and-he-claimed that-they [are] thus because-they use things [that] not not said-them ever of the-dialecticians in the-dialectic: in-manner-of what [is] in the-hall which [is] from the-direction, not from the-?; and-in-manner-of the-saying the-saying that from-you you also indeed you-were thing some; and-in-manner-of the-saying the-saying that Achilles he [is] for-the-sake-of, not he [is] for-the-sake-of Achilles; and-things many of likes-of these, how-many they-were.
