# text = فاما الكبير فهو ان يستعمل كل واحد واحد من هذه التى وصفت على مجرى الاليق والاشبه وان يستعمل اسما مضعفة والالسن وان يكون من ما يتادا وينتقل هو عظيم كبير
# transliteration = fa-ammā l-kabīru fa-huwa an yastaʿmila kulla wāḥidin wāḥidin min hādhihi allatī wuṣifat ʿalā majrā l-alyaqi wa-l-ashbahi wa-an yastaʿmila asmāʾan muḍaʿʿafatan wa-l-alsuna wa-an yakūna min mā yataʾaddā wa-yantaqilu huwa ʿaẓīmun kabīrun
# prose_translation = What is great is that one use each single one of these things described in the most fitting and most apt way, and that one use doubled nouns and "tongues"; and that [one's diction] be of what is transferred and carried over — that is very great.
# literal_translation = So-as-for the-great, so-it [is] that he-use each one one of these which were-described upon course-of the-most-fitting and-the-most-apt, and-that he-use nouns doubled and-the-tongues; and-that it-be of what is-transferred and-is-carried-over, it [is] great big.
