# text = وهى اليق واصلح فى اثرواٮٯو هو النشيد من جميع ما وصف واما فى ايانبو فمن قبل انها تتشبه باللفظ وهذه الاسما تصلح وتليق بمقدار ما يستعمل بها الانسان على طريق وهذه هى الحقيقى المتادى والمسمى بالسرٮانية صڡٮاٮٮا ماخوذ من الاتمام
# transliteration = wa-hiya alyaqu wa-aṣlaḥu fī athrwā?qū(?) huwa l-nashīdu min jamīʿi mā wuṣifa wa-ammā fī īyānbū fa-min qibali annahā tatashabbahu bi-l-lafẓi wa-hādhihi l-asmāʾu taṣluḥu wa-talīqu bi-miqdāri mā yastaʿmilu bihā l-insānu ʿalā ṭarīqin wa-hādhihi hiya l-ḥaqīqiyyu l-mutaʾaddī wa-l-musammā bi-l-suryāniyyati ṣ??ā??ā(?) maʾkhūdhun mina l-itmāmi
# prose_translation = They are more fitting and more suitable in the heroic (?) — that is, the song — than all that has been described. As for iambos, since it imitates speech, these nouns suit and fit it to the extent that a man uses them in [ordinary] fashion (?); and these are the proper, the transferred, and what is called in Syriac […] (?), taken from "completion".
# literal_translation = And-they [are] more-fitting and-more-suitable in heroic? — it [is] the-song — than all what was-described; and-as-for in iambos, so-from account-of that-it imitates the-diction, and-these the-nouns suit and-fit in-measure-of what uses with-them the-man upon way; and-these they [are] the-proper, the-transferred, and-the-named in-the-Syriac ?, taken from the-completion.
