# text = اما فى سالامانا فحروب المراكب وفى سيقيليا حرب الڡركوٮٮا ڡـ*ں كلى هذين ليسا شى احر غير انها تنتهى الى انقضا واحد واحد وكذلك فى الازمنة التى **ٮ بعد فى وقت بعد وقت يكون واحد منها الذى لا يكون له شى اخر هو اخر واىقصـ*
# transliteration = ammā fī Sālāmānā fa-ḥurūbu l-marākibi wa-fī Sīqīliyā ḥarbu l-Qarkūniyā(?) fa-inna(?) kilā hādhayni laysā shayʾan ākhara(?) ghayra annahā tantahī ilā inqiḍāʾin wāḥidin wāḥidin wa-kadhālika fī l-azminati allatī **t baʿdu fī waqtin baʿda waqtin yakūnu wāḥidun minhā alladhī lā yakūnu lahū shayʾun ākharu huwa ākhirun wa-inqiḍāʾun(?)
# prose_translation = As for at Salamis, [there were] the battles of the ships, and in Sicily the war of the Carthaginians (?); for (?) both of these are not another thing (?), except that they end each in its own single completion. And likewise in the times which […] afterwards, at one time after another, one of them comes about which has no other thing that is an end and completion (?).
# literal_translation = As-for in Salamis, so-battles-of the-ships, and-in Sicily war-of the-Carthaginians(?); so-verily(?) both these-two are-not thing other(?), except that-they end to completion one one; and-likewise in the-times which [...] after, in time after time is one of-them which not is to-it thing other, it [is] end and-completion(?).
