# sent_id = 23.7
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 23.7
# translation_lang = en
# text = ولذلك عمل اليادا واودوسيا كلتيهما مديحا واحدا او بعد كر اثنتين واما *** المعروفة ٮٯوٯواٮٮا فكثيرة والى الاليادا الصغيرة فثمانية واكثر التى تقال السلاح منها المعروفة ٮٮااوفطلامس وفيلوقطيطس المعروف بافطوخيلا وكبس الياس ورجوع المراكب واسين وطرواس
# transliteration = wa-li-dhālika ʿamila Iliyādā wa-Ūdūsiyā kiltayhimā madīḥan wāḥidan aw baʿda karrin(?) ithnatayni wa-ammā *** al-maʿrūfatu ?qūfūwā??ā(?) fa-kathīratun wa-ilā l-Aliyādā l-ṣaghīrati fa-thamāniyatun wa-aktharu allatī tuqālu l-silāḥu minhā l-maʿrūfatu ??āwfṭlāmis(?) wa-Fīlūqṭīṭis al-maʿrūfu bi-Afṭūkhīlā wa-kabsu Ilyās wa-rujūʿu l-marākibi wa-Asīn wa-Ṭrūās
# prose_translation = Therefore he made the Iliad and the Odyssey, each of them, into one praise, or two after repetition (?); as for […] the one known as the Cypria (?), [the praises from it] are many, and from the Little Iliad eight and more: that among them which is called "The Arms"; the one known as Neoptolemus (?); Philoctetes, known as Afṭūkhīlā; the storming of Ilium; the return of the ships; Sinon; and the Trojan women.
# literal_translation = And-for-that he-made Iliad and-Odyssey, both-of-them, praise one, or after repetition(?) two; and-as-for [...] the-known [as] Cypria(?), so-many; and-to the-Iliad the-little, so-eight and-more: which is-said the-arms of-them; the-known [as] Neoptolemus(?); and-Philoctetes the-known by-Afṭūkhīlā; and-storming-of Ilium; and-return-of the-ships; and-Sinon; and-Trojan-women.
