# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 24.3
# translation_lang = en
# text = يستعملها اوميروس اول السمرا وعلى الكفاية وذلك ان شعر كلتيهما هو مركب واما ايليدا فبسيطة وانفعالية واما القصيدة فمركبة وهى الذى تدل بالكلية على العادات ومع هذه هى دالة باللفظ والذهن على كل فعل
# transliteration = yastaʿmiluhā Ūmīrūs awwala l-sumarāʾi wa-ʿalā l-kifāyati wa-dhālika anna shiʿra kiltayhimā huwa murakkabun wa-ammā Īlīdā fa-basīṭatun wa-infiʿāliyyatun wa-ammā l-qaṣīdatu fa-murakkabatun wa-hiya alladhī tadullu bi-l-kulliyyati ʿalā l-ʿādāti wa-maʿa hādhihi hiya dāllatun bi-l-lafẓi wa-l-dhihni ʿalā kulli fiʿlin
# prose_translation = Homer uses them, first of the storytellers, and adequately; for the poetry of both of them is composite: the Iliad is simple and passional, while the ode is complex, and it is what indicates the characters throughout; and besides this it indicates every action through expression and thought.
# literal_translation = Uses-them Homer, first-of the-storytellers, and-upon the-sufficiency; and-that [is] that poetry-of both-of-them it [is] composite: and-as-for Iliad, so-simple and-passional; and-as-for the-ode, so-complex, and-it [is] that-which indicates in-the-entirety upon the-characters; and-with this it [is] indicating by-the-expression and-the-mind upon every action.
