# text = واما اوميروس فهو مستحق للمديح والتفريط فى اشيا اخر تفريطا كثيرا اذ كان هو وحده فقط من بين جميع الشعرا ليس يذهب عليه ما ينبغى ان يفعل
# transliteration = wa-ammā Ūmīrūs fa-huwa mustaḥiqqun li-l-madīḥi wa-l-tafrīṭi fī ashyāʾa ukhara tafrīṭan kathīran idh kāna huwa waḥdahū faqaṭ min bayni jamīʿi l-shuʿarāʾi laysa yadhhabu ʿalayhi mā yanbaghī an yafʿala
# prose_translation = As for Homer, he deserves praise and extolling (?) in other things, greatly so, since he alone among all the poets is not unaware of what he ought to do.
# literal_translation = And-as-for Homer, so-he [is] deserving of-the-praise and-the-extolling(?) in things other, extolling much, since was he, alone-he only, from among all the-poets, not escapes upon-him what it-is-fitting that he-do.
