# sent_id = 24.14
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 24.14
# translation_lang = en
# text = وقد ينبغى للشاعر ان يكون ما يتكلم به يسيرا قليلا وذلك انه ليس هو فى مشبه محاكى فاما الشعرا الاخر فمنهم من يجاهده جدا ويكون به تشبيه وحكاية فى اشيا ٮسٮٮه واما ذلك فمن حيث انما عمل صدرا يسيرا فهو *** على الحال رجل او امراة او عادة فى حكايته من ساعته من حيث لا ياتى ***لك بشى لم يعتاد لكن ما قد اعتيد
# transliteration = wa-qad yanbaghī li-l-shāʿiri an yakūna mā yatakallamu bihī yasīran qalīlan wa-dhālika annahū laysa huwa fī mushabbihin muḥākī fa-ammā l-shuʿarāʾu l-ukharu fa-minhum man yujāhiduhū jiddan wa-yakūnu bihī tashbīhun wa-ḥikāyatun fī ashyāʾa ?s??a wa-ammā dhālika fa-min ḥaythu innamā ʿamila ṣadran yasīran fa-huwa *** ʿalā l-ḥāli rajulun aw imraʾatun aw ʿādatun fī ḥikāyatihī min sāʿatihī min ḥaythu lā yaʾtī ***lk bi-shayʾin lam yuʿtad lākin mā qad uʿtīda
# prose_translation = The poet ought to make what he says little and slight; for in this he is not an imitating likener. As for the other poets, among them is one who strives at it greatly, and there is likening and narration by him in […] things. As for that one, inasmuch as he made only a short opening, he […] at once a man or a woman or a character in his narration, immediately, inasmuch as he does not bring […] anything unaccustomed, but what has been accustomed.
# literal_translation = And-indeed it-is-fitting for-the-poet that be what he-speaks with-it little slight; and-that [is] that-he is-not he in likener imitating. So-as-for the-poets the-others, so-of-them [is] who strives-it very, and-is by-him likening and-narration in things [...]. And-as-for that-one, so-from where only he-made opening short, so-he [...] upon the-state man or woman or character in his-narration from his-hour, from where not he-brings [...] with-thing not accustomed but what indeed was-accustomed.
