# prose_translation = After these, [things] are brought toward the rout of Hector, just as mockeries and laughable things are brought on the stage, inasmuch as it is seen: as for some of them, he, while standing, stopped and does not pursue, and follows the dead (?); and as for that one, inasmuch as he swaggers (?). But in epic it is hidden and not perceived.
# literal_translation = And-from after these is-brought with-them toward rout-of Hector, as is-brought in the-dwelling the-mockeries and-the-laughables, from where is-seen: as-for some-of-them, and-he [is] standing, stopped and-not pursues and-follows the-dead(?); and-as-for that-one, so-from where he-swaggers(?); and-as-for in epic, so-indeed is-hidden and-not is-perceived with-it.
