# text = واما الاسما التى ضربت من التادية وهى من التادية هى ايضا كما يقول اوميروس الرجال الاخر واللهة متسلحة على الخيل كانوا رقادين الليل كله وقال مع ذلك امن حيث كانوا اليونانيون مجتمعين فى صحراة طرواس واجتمع بينهم ٮٮات وشى وسوٮٮاٮ وصفرات الزمر وذلك ان هذه باجمعها بحسب التادية انما قيلت بدل من الكثير
# transliteration = wa-ammā l-asmāʾu allatī ḍuribat mina l-taʾdiyati wa-hiya mina l-taʾdiyati hiya ayḍan kamā yaqūlu Ūmīrūs al-rijālu l-ukharu wa-l-ālihatu mutasalliḥatan ʿalā l-khayli kānū ruqqādīna l-layla kullahū wa-qāla maʿa dhālika amin ḥaythu kānū l-yūnāniyyūna mujtamiʿīna fī ṣaḥrāti Ṭarwās wa-jtamaʿa baynahum nāyātun(?) wa-shayʾun wa-sw??ā?(?) wa-ṣafarātu l-zamri wa-dhālika anna hādhihi bi-ajmaʿihā bi-ḥasabi l-taʾdiyati innamā qīlat badalan mina l-kathīri
# prose_translation = As for the nouns that were coined by metaphor, and they are of metaphor, they too are as Homer says: "The other men and the gods, armed on horses, were sleeping the whole night"; and he said along with that: "when the Greeks were gathered in the plain of Troy, and there gathered among them reed-pipes (?) and something and […] and the whistlings of the pipe". That is because all these were said, according to metaphor, only in place of "the many".
# literal_translation = And-as-for the-names which were-struck from the-metaphor, and-they [are] from the-metaphor, they also [are] as says Homer: the-men the-other and-the-gods, armed upon the-horses, were sleeping the-night all-of-it; and-he-said with that: when were the-Greeks gathered in plain-of Troy, and-gathered among-them reed-pipes(?) and-thing and-[?] and-whistlings-of the-pipe; and-that [is] that these in-their-entirety according-to the-metaphor only were-said instead of the-many.
