# prose_translation = As for the noun "life", it is divided. Empedocles too says that those who had never ceased to be im[mortal] were at once coming to be mortal; and as for "life", it is what was created for them of old.
# literal_translation = And-as-for noun-of the-life, so-it-is-divided; and-Empedocles also says that-it: were those-who not ceased other-than mortal since ever arising from their-hour mortal; and-as-for the-life, so-which was-created for-them anciently.
