# subdoc = 25.21
# translation_lang = en
# text = واما التى قالها بحسب عادة المقولة ڡكما يقول فى الشراب انه ممتزج ومن هاهنا *عمل ما للساق المصوعة من الرصاص والحدادين وايضا من هاهنا يقال الغانوميدس شرب الشراب لا انه يشرب للشراب من قبل ا**** بحسب التادية ايضا
# transliteration = wa-ammā allatī qālahā bi-ḥasabi ʿādati l-maqūlati fa-kamā yaqūlu fī l-sharābi innahū mumtazijun wa-min hāhunā *uʿmalu mā li-l-sāqi l-maṣūghati(?) mina l-raṣāṣi wa-l-ḥaddādīna wa-ayḍan min hāhunā yuqālu l-Ghānūmīdis shariba l-sharāba lā annahū yashrabu li-l-sharābi min qibali a**** bi-ḥasabi l-taʾdiyati ayḍan
# prose_translation = As for those which he said according to the custom of diction, it is as he says of the drink that it is mixed; and from here is made (?) what belongs to the leg, wrought (?) of lead, and the smiths; and again from here it is said that Ganymede drank the drink, not that he drinks for the drink, because […] according to metaphor too.
# literal_translation = And-as-for which he-said-them according-to custom-of the-diction, so-as he-says in the-drink that-it [is] mixed; and-from here is-made(?) what [is] for-the-leg the-wrought(?) from the-lead and-the-smiths; and-also from here is-said the-Ganymede drank the-drink, not that-he drinks for-the-drink, from account-of […] according-to the-metaphor also.
