# text = حتى يظن الانسان خاصة بغلوقس انه ضد هذا وايضا لا الافراد منهم يريدون وياخذون بغير نطق من حيث يحكمون لهم ايضا ويعملون قياسا و** انهم قالوا انه يظن الذين يبكتون ان ذلك يعمله هو ضد
# transliteration = ḥattā yaẓunna l-insānu khāṣṣatan Bighlūqus annahū ḍiddu hādhā wa-ayḍan lā l-afrādu minhum yurīdūna wa-yaʾkhudhūna bi-ghayri nuṭqin min ḥaythu yaḥkumūna lahum ayḍan wa-yaʿmalūna qiyāsan wa-** annahum qālū innahū yaẓunnu alladhīna yubakkitūna anna dhālika yaʿmaluhū huwa ḍiddun
# prose_translation = … so that one might think, especially Glaucon (?), that it is the opposite of this. Again, not (?) the individuals among them intend and take [things] without reason, inasmuch as they also pass judgement for themselves and make a syllogism; and […] that they said: those who censure think that what he does is contrary.
