# sent_id = 25.25
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 25.25
# translation_lang = en
# text = وانما كان ساب هذا اهرٯارس وذلك انهم كانوا يظنون به انه لاقوناى فمن القبيح الا يكون يلقاه طيلاماخس فى لاقادامونيا عند ما صار الى هنالك ولعل هنالك كما قال اهل قادلينس و*ر انهم قالوا ان عندهم عمل اودوساوس وايقاريس الاساسات من قبل ان ذلك حق
# transliteration = wa-innamā kāna sābu(?) hādhā Ahrqāris(?) wa-dhālika annahum kānū yaẓunnūna bihī annahū Lāqūnāy fa-mina l-qabīḥi allā yakūna yalqāhu Ṭīlāmākhus fī Lāqādāmūniyā ʿinda mā ṣāra ilā hunālika wa-laʿalla hunālika kamā qāla ahlu Qādlīnus wa-*r annahum qālū inna ʿindahum ʿamila Ūdūsāwus wa-Īqārīs al-asāsāti min qibali anna dhālika ḥaqqun
# prose_translation = The cause (?) of this was only Icarius (?): they used to think of him that he was a Laconian, so it is absurd that Telemachus should not meet him in Lacedaemon when he went there. But perhaps there it is as the people of Cephallenia (?) said; and […] that they said that among them Odysseus and Icarius made the foundations (?), because that is true.
# literal_translation = And-only was cause(?)-of this Icarius(?); and-that [is] that-they were thinking of-him that-he [is] Laconian; so-from the-ugly that-not be meets-him Telemachus in Lacedaemon when went to there; and-perhaps there [it is] as said people-of Cephallenia, and-[…] that-they said that among-them made Odysseus and-Icarius the-foundations, from account-of that that [is] true.
