# sent_id = 26.4
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 26.4
# translation_lang = en
# text = ومثل هذا المديح هو كما احتسب القدما والذين اتوا بالاخرة من بعدهم مرايين منافقين من قبل انهم افضل كثيرا من عالاس كما كان يلقب مٮٮٮٯوس ٯاٯٮدس و*عتمد الاعتقاد من فنٮدارس واما ان يكون لهذه اليه [ومن حيث هو من *لودا] وفى جميع الصناعة يكون حاله عند صنعة افى
# transliteration = wa-mithlu hādhā l-madīḥu huwa kamā iḥtasaba l-qudamāʾu wa-lladhīna ataw bi-l-ākhirati min baʿdihim murāʾīna munāfiqīna min qibali annahum afḍalu kathīran min ʿālās kamā kāna yulaqqibu M???qūs(?) Qāq?dis(?) wa-*ʿtamada l-iʿtiqāda min Fin?dāris wa-ammā an yakūna li-hādhihi ilayhi [wa-min ḥaythu huwa min *lūdā] wa-fī jamīʿi l-ṣināʿati yakūnu ḥāluhū ʿinda ṣanʿati afī
# prose_translation = Like this is praise (tragedy): it is as the ancients, and those who came later after them, reckoned [them] ostentatious hypocrites, because they are much better than ʿālās (?), as M[ynniscus] (?) used to call Q[allippides] (?); and the belief was relied upon (?) from Pindarus. As for its being [related] for these to it [and inasmuch as it is from …], in the whole art its state is [that] toward the art of epic.
# literal_translation = And-like this [is] the-praise: it [is] as reckoned the-ancients and-those-who came at-the-last from after-them ostentatious hypocrites, from account-of that-they [are] better much than ʿālās(?), as was calling M[…]s Q[…]s; and-relied(?) the-belief from Pindarus; and-as-for that be for-these to-it [and-from where it [is] from […]], and-in all the-art is its-state with art-of epic.
