# transliteration = wa-dhālika anna ḥāla ṣanʿati afī ʿinda l-nāẓirīna yaqūlūna alladhīna laysa bi-l-muḥtājīna ilā shayʾin mina l-ashkāli innahum ṭiyābun jiddan *ṣināʿatu l-madīḥi ʿinda l-muzayyafīna wa-fa-ammā furūṭīqī fa-ẓāhirun annahā akhassu
# prose_translation = That is because the state of the art of epic is with the spectators (they say) who have no need of any of the gestures, that they are very good; [while] the art of praise is with the counterfeit ones. As for phortikē, then, it is evident that it is baser.
# literal_translation = And-that [is] that state-of art-of epic [is] with the-spectators, they-say, those-who not-are with-the-needing to thing of the-shapes, that-they [are] good very; [and-]art-of the-praise [is] with the-counterfeit-ones; and-so-as-for phortikē, so-evident [is] that-it [is] baser.
