# sent_id = 26.12
# document_id = 0086-034
# text_lang = ara
# subdoc = 26.12
# translation_lang = en
# text = وايضا التى هى مختلفة فى الطول ليكون اخر الشبيه والحكاية وذلك ان كون هذه خاصة بغتة اكثر من كونها كذلك وهى ممتزجة فى زمان كثير واعنى بذلك مثل ان يضع الانسان اوفيدس لذلك الذى وضعه سوفاقلس فى الافى التى له فى هذه التى ايليدا هى فيها
# transliteration = wa-ayḍan allatī hiya mukhtalifatun fī l-ṭūli li-yakūna ākhiru l-shabīhi wa-l-ḥikāyati wa-dhālika anna kawna hādhihi khāṣṣatan baghtatan aktharu min kawnihā kadhālika wa-hiya mumtazijatun fī zamānin kathīrin wa-aʿnī bi-dhālika mithla an yaḍaʿa l-insānu Ūfīdis li-dhālika alladhī waḍaʿahū Sūfāqlis fī l-afī allatī lahū fī hādhihi allatī Īlīdā hiya fīhā
# prose_translation = Again, that which differs in length, so that the end of the likeness and imitation may be [reached]; for this being, especially, all at once is more [pleasant] than its being so while diluted over much time. I mean by that, for example, a man's putting the Oedipus, the one Sophocles composed, into the epic which is his, into these in which the Iliad is.
# literal_translation = And-also which it [is] different in the-length, so-that be end-of the-likeness and-the-imitation; and-that [is] that being-of this especially sudden [is] more than its-being likewise, and-it [is] mixed in time much; and-I-mean by-that like that puts the-man Oedipus, for-that which composed-it Sophocles, in the-epic which [is] to-him, in these which the-Iliad, it [is] in-them.
